{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem","id":1123755,"title":"Pure Breed Problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-01T20:38:41-07:00","id":1123755,"title":"Pure Breed Problem","content":"While working on a game of WtA, I had a player bring up some serious concerns about the Pure Breed trait. They think it's dumb, and the mechanical bonuses illogical. In their words:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The queen can be the queen all she wants. If she walks up and kicks my dog and slaps my kid. I'm gonna beat her to a pulp. All the noble breeding in the word is not gonna stop that. And will not give her any benefit at all.<br /> <br /> If a pure blood garou of any level, walks up and just breaks their neck, are either of your characters gonna care at all about their lineage? Or will they frenzy and make garou paste. any onlookers too, can't care at all about random murder. so screw the bonus dice to whatever would be involved.<br /> <br /> It's all social interaction, which, according to the entry, is unlimited and unstipulated if its social and involves garou. You win, no matter what, and that's my point. That is wrong. If the book elaborated, and said if its an unjust or dishonorable stance, then you LOSE dice equal to your pureblood rating, then yes, I could probably get behind it, but for it to always be a plus, no matter what, is flawed and stupid. </div> </div> </div>They'd prefer for it to be removed from the game. Thoughts on this? It's not the first time I've heard people claim PB is broken, or doesn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":12874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","user":"Mongoose","date":". 08-01-2017, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T22:08:02-07:00","id":1123769,"title":"","content":"The only thing you'd really lose in the setting is the obvious mechanical advantage of the Silver Fangs being the alpha tribe. Without Pure Breed to bolster their Social Rolls, it would be much easier to ignore them and thus effectively dethrone them. But other than that, it's not like the game falls apart.<br /> <br /> However, one of the major themes of the game is that the characters who get the most advantage out of Pure Breed may not actually be the ones who make the best leaders or actually deserve this kind of status. When some obvious high Pure Breed Garou (most likely Silver Fangs, but most tribes have some members with high Pure Breed) shows up and takes over simply as a result of these extra dice, it is unjust and it is resented.<br /> <br /> And that tension can be fun to roleplay through even if the PC(s) get the short stick end of that. That dynamic does add something to the game, and I like that. One of the pleasures of playing a Bone Gnawer is to be outright contemptuous of those kind of unjust &quot;tricks&quot;.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed is a function of supernatural power of some kind (as it only occurs as a result of the tribe's totem) so it may be &quot;illogical&quot;, but only in the way any other kind of mind or emotion controlling power is. Pure Breed represents a connection to a higher spiritual world and it is this experience of the numinous which results in social deference from those who don't have it to those who do.<br /> <br /> I don't think Pure Breed is broken in the context of the game as your players do. Although I do understand them not liking the idea that their PC who has no Pure Breed is at a supreme disadvantage in social contests with an NPC with five extra dice because their character has Pure Breed 5. (Although there are ways to mechanically compensate for it to a degree - using Ancestors to get more dice, spending XP to boost the most important social traits, spending Willpower for successes). But ultimately this seems to be a complaint that &quot;I don't like the fact that my character would be disadvantaged in certain situations.&quot; Well, that sucks of course, but some games are &quot;unfair&quot; like that. If you play Vampire and have a character with bad Generation (13th as opposed to 8th), you have all sorts of negatives accordingly. That is just part of that game. And yes, I've heard many players complain about Generation as well for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> To modern people, the idea that the &quot;lower classes&quot; would automatically &quot;defer&quot; to their &quot;betters&quot; is extremely hard to understand or tolerate, but wasn't uncommon even half a century or ago. Even in cases where you had peasants revolts and the like, in cases where they actually negotiated with kings of nobles, they spoke very respectfully for the most part. Only in severe cases of massive social change did things get topsy turvy (like in the French or Russian Revolutions) and such status privileges become completely overthrown.<br /> <br /> But I'm not quite sure what your players are arguing about. Yes, of course, if another Garou (even with Pure Breed) physically abuses or kills another Garou, it makes perfect sense why the encounter would go into physical combat and ignore social challenges. So what? The higher Pure Breed Garou know that. Only an idiot would push certain things to the point where justifiable violence against them could be pursued. Does the player think any Social Challenge is meaningless because the other party could always resort to violence? Probably not. Certainly society distinguishes which situations should not result in violence, and which situations where violence is either accepted, tolerated, excused, or otherwise justified.<br /> <br /> The flip side to Pure Breed is not that there is negative game mechanic social penalty if the Garou does not upheld their standard. The flip side is that high Pure Breed Garou have a social obligation to act accordingly. And if they don't, Garou do become resentful against them, dislike them, form conspiracies against them, or begin to disagree publicly against them - and that includes other high Pure Breed Garou, not just the lower breeds. But this is more in the realm of the ST reacting to what happens in game than giving an automatic penalty. This is one of the major reasons why more and more Garou are unhappy about the leadership of the Silver Fangs - it explains why the Shadow Lords and others are looking to make a change which is a major element in the setting. And it is one reason why the Bone Gnawers are always pissed off against the other tribes.<br /> <br /> Rather than doing away with Pure Breed mechanics, you may want to discuss with your players how you may handle those situations where high Pure Breed Garou develop a bad reputation for failing to act like they should. Maybe you might give them a penalty to the Difficulty numbers to certain or all Garou who know that werewolf does not measure up. Or allow a system where PB dice decline according to differences in Rank. Or saying if the Garou spends WP he can ignore the effects of PB for that challenge or even whole scene (since WP is a finite resource, I personally like to allow players to use it for various reasons - if it is important to them they have that option, but since regaining WP during a story is generally hard PCs have to think hard about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T06:20:14-07:00","id":1123850,"title":"","content":"If they want it to be more circumstantial, that's probably pretty doable. Just have it apply to Changer business and not casual interactions, or use one of the ideas from the Apocalypse/Forsaken conversion guide and have it reduce the Renown that you get for any given reward, minimum 1, because the lineage of the heroes of the tribe demands more impressive deeds. Because that's what PB is, and needs to be renamed - recognition by the spirits that your predecessors have a great and impressive history of heroics in the tribe. The moment you switch tribes? You lose all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T06:53:09-07:00","id":1123860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem#post1123755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While working on a game of WtA, I had a player bring up some serious concerns about the Pure Breed trait. They think it's dumb, and the mechanical bonuses illogical. In their words:<br /> <br /> They'd prefer for it to be removed from the game. Thoughts on this? It's not the first time I've heard people claim PB is broken, or doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, here's how I explained it in my game.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pure Breed is racist and classicist. This is probably the most direct way to explain this and it doesn't reflect well on the Garou. However, there's no real way to dance around this without facing it. The newly turned cub of the Silver Fangs who has never fought a Black Spiral Dancer or cleansed a corrupted caern has pure white fur and blue eyes. You know what that means? Every time he speaks, he will probably be listened to before you. If he beats you up, he'll be believed. If you beat him up, you'll be killed. Why? BECAUSE THE WORLD IS NOT FAIR. Wow, a warrior society based on ancestry and heritage is actually dickish. Who would have thought. It's the World of Darkness, not the world of furry superheroes.</span></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:02:04-07:00","id":1123911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem#post1123755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd prefer for it to be removed from the game. Thoughts on this? It's not the first time I've heard people claim PB is broken, or doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few different issues here.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;broken&quot; issue, the baseline rules are a bit extreme in bonus with a very ST whim penalty with not mechanical or even general rule to structure a drawback on. This is made worse by any number of Gifts and Merits that can add even more dice or reduce the difficulty of social rolls. This is, however, the easier part of it to fix. W20 Rage Across the World, introduces both the Sept Standing Background (which lets characters, at least for their home Sept, earn bonus dice to compete with Pure-Breed), and a cap on the total Background/Merit bonus dice you can apply to a single roll at 5 above your base-line roll (so if you have 6 dice, but are currently at a -2 penalty, you can benefit +7 from social Backgrounds and Merits to cancel the -2, but anything more would be wasted). This addition alone takes a lot of the wind out of complaints about Pure-Breed. Adding in something to enforce the idea that Pure-Breed means having to live up to expectations should pretty much address any lingering problems. You definitely don't need to remove it.<br /> <br /> The issue with it not making any sense is boiled into the fact that it's two different concepts smashed together and the compromise is always lacking in narrative logic. PB is both a physical (for a supernatural being) trait that governs looks and progeny, and a mystical trait that confers social authority. By choosing to link/maintain the linking of these two concepts, PB has always had counter intuitive issues attached to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123769#post1123769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the pleasures of playing a Bone Gnawer is to be outright contemptuous of those kind of unjust &quot;tricks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, the rules let them roll into your good graces such that you like them anyway. A high PB character with Notable Heritage and Supporter rolls in, makes some grand speech about unity and working together - under their plans and leadership of course - and with +x dice and -3 diff, it's almost impossible for a PC Gnawer to avoid being swayed. The rules let you easily circumvent the intended results (as you communicate later in this post) where dissent over PB is common... because you can social roll away that dissent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But ultimately this seems to be a complaint that &quot;I don't like the fact that my character would be disadvantaged in certain situations.&quot; </div> </div> </div>But it's not &quot;certain situations.&quot; It's, &quot;all social situations between Garou.&quot; A screw up Silver Fang doesn't lose those dice, and can social steamroll any dissent into forgiving them and such. PB mechanically actually detracts from any fun of playing the classist aspects of Garou society by making those without it unable to maintain ill-will to resent it as well as being at a disadvantage in the first place. In VtM, a vampire that tosses Dominate around too much is in for a lot of retribution, because Dominate can't make people like you while you're making them obey you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To modern people, the idea that the &quot;lower classes&quot; would automatically &quot;defer&quot; to their &quot;betters&quot; is extremely hard to understand or tolerate, but wasn't uncommon even half a century or ago. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that +X dice like PB grants really models this sort of deference. There's a huge difference between public displays of accepting social norms, and actually giving more credence to someone for having the right parents. The Litany does a lot more to enforce this sort of behavior than PB does (which seems appropriate to me anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm not quite sure what your players are arguing about. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the core point is, &quot;A PB character can publicly murder another Garou and they still get all their bonus dice.&quot; they don't lose those dice for failure to live up to their breeding. The player's examples might be a bit extreme, but the point is mostly that the only way to lose PB is to leave your Tribe even when it makes no sense for you to keep those dice because your character is being a complete asshat.<br /> <br /> Yes, of course, if another Garou (even with Pure Breed) physically abuses or kills another Garou, it makes perfect sense why the encounter would go into physical combat and ignore social challenges. So what? The higher Pure Breed Garou know that. Only an idiot would push certain things to the point where justifiable violence against them could be pursued. Does the player think any Social Challenge is meaningless because the other party could always resort to violence? Probably not. Certainly society distinguishes which situations should not result in violence, and which situations where violence is either accepted, tolerated, excused, or otherwise justified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123850#post1123850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just have it apply to Changer business and not casual interactions,...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably a bit too subjective for most people's play. The line between &quot;business&quot; and &quot;casual interactions,&quot; is pretty slim with a culture like the Garou Nation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123860#post1123860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here's how I explained it in my game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's worth remembering that it's a game we play to have fun. Not everyone wants to have classist themes shoved down their throats with mechanics, and be told that disliking that makes them not really buying into the &quot;dark&quot; of the game. Human society IRL has plenty of dark issues with classism without certain families being supernaturally awesome at social stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T11:46:53-07:00","id":1123958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123911#post1123911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's worth remembering that it's a game we play to have fun. Not everyone wants to have classist themes shoved down their throats with mechanics, and be told that disliking that makes them not really buying into the &quot;dark&quot; of the game. Human society IRL has plenty of dark issues with classism without certain families being supernaturally awesome at social stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can play the game however you want but it is a HORROR game. Pure Breed is not REMOTELY the most horrific element of the game, it is a way your player character can get a bunch of bonus dice for causing people to pay more attention to you while also making a bunch of nobles snootier about the fact they're better bred than Bonegnawers. Also, do you know who has the same themes of &quot;Pure Blood&quot; vs &quot;Mud Blood&quot;--FRIGGING HARRY POTTER.<br /> <br /> If you dislike Pure Breed as a merit, take note it really just makes a bunch of werewolves into Draco Malfoy.<br /> <br /> Which seems an odd thing to worry about in a game where you may murder a diner full of innocents because your rage got of our control.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:13:38-07:00","id":1123988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123911#post1123911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, the rules let them roll into your good graces such that you like them anyway. A high PB character with Notable Heritage and Supporter rolls in, makes some grand speech about unity and working together - under their plans and leadership of course - and with +x dice and -3 diff, it's almost impossible for a PC Gnawer to avoid being swayed. The rules let you easily circumvent the intended results (as you communicate later in this post) where dissent over PB is common... because you can social roll away that dissent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But it's not &quot;certain situations.&quot; It's, &quot;all social situations between Garou.&quot; A screw up Silver Fang doesn't lose those dice, and can social steamroll any dissent into forgiving them and such. PB mechanically actually detracts from any fun of playing the classist aspects of Garou society by making those without it unable to maintain ill-will to resent it as well as being at a disadvantage in the first place. In VtM, a vampire that tosses Dominate around too much is in for a lot of retribution, because Dominate can't make people like you while you're making them obey you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree because I don't think Social Rolls are as powerful as you seem to describe. There are practical limits in what a Social Roll can accomplish and this can change over time or in different circumstances. Having high social skill is not the same as magical mind control.<br /> <br /> Something as simple as &quot;Can you open this door for me?&quot; should lead to very different results depending whether you are talking to a hotel employee as you enter the building, another passerby as you enter a store, a person alone in their home confronted with someone they don't know asking to be let into the house late or night, or a security guard under orders not to let anybody in. You can go from - &quot;no roll is needed, you are let in&quot; to &quot;OK, roll with standard difficulty&quot; to &quot;The person isn't going to let you in. I won't even allow a roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> In real life I have seen some circumstances where one person has - in game terms - a big dice pool for Social Rolls, and there are others with a much smaller dice pool. Yet it becomes obvious over time that this one person is actually a selfish jerk, a sociopath, or simply someone whose values are beyond the pale (say a Holocaust Denier). In the beginning, before this truth is actually realized, the person with the big social dice pool is quite successful with getting people to agree with him, do what he wants to do, or simply like him. But over time people begin to learn the truth about this person and begin to feel exploited, ignored, used, or become appalled. They begin to challenge that person - hoping the person is actually reasonable, concerned, or just misunderstood.<br /> <br /> Now because that person is highly skilled socially, he often or even always &quot;wins&quot; these arguments. But the &quot;win&quot; is usually just that the other person doesn't know what to say. They can't articulate it in a way that causes them to win the argument because the other person is so skilled at rhetoric. No matter what they say, they'll ultimately feel like an idiot and often begin to simply say nothing at all. But at the same time, they aren't actually convinced by this person - they just don't know how to respond effectively in rhetoric. Even while these people are silent and not disputing the other person (or disputing very poorly), it is obvious they actually are not convinced and are seething in resentment or outrage. In many cases, they are looking around the room or table and hoping someone else, anyone else, will step up and smack the crap out of this guy orally.<br /> <br /> At that point in time, no matter how charming or persuasive this person is, people begin to react in ways that they ignore his high social skills. In some cases they simply ostracize the person and remove them from their social circle. In other cases, they simply put up their shields and simply zone out the other person when they begin to act in these offending ways. Despite this person effectively &quot;winning&quot; the argument tactically, they actually fail to convince anyone. In these situations, what I've seen is that if there is someone new to the group and scene and observes this, they are usually convinced or at least have a favorable impression of the jerk. These new guys haven't become &quot;immune&quot; to his charm, and therefore don't know why the group is treating this guy so badly or ignoring well made points. Their learning curve is just beginning, but they will get there eventually. In some cases, the person is actually threatened and told to leave him or the entire group alone.<br /> <br /> In other words, if someone treats you like crap, no matter how skilled he is socially, you KNOW he is treating you like crap. If someone is recommending a course of action that will get you killed for no reason, a mutiny will result of some kind barring some other reason that keeps their loyalty outside of that person. Someone who is a Holocaust Denier, no matter how charming or skilled with words, won't actually convince you the Holocaust didn't happen - even if your own lack of knowledge and debate skills makes you lose that argument on a theoretical points basis.<br /> <br /> These kinds of people don't become unstoppable social steamrollers. Instead they usually have to move from social circle to social circle as they burn the relationships they have with others and need to find new victims. If they do have a group of friends who stay with them, it is usually people who already want to do or believe what this guy wants, or sycophants who are attracted to bullies.<br /> <br /> Garou with high Pure Breed are in the exact same dynamic.<br /> <br /> Yes, a jerk Garou with high Pure Breed can steamroll dissent - but only selectively, or in the very beginning, or for a little while. If the person is clearly acting against the interests of their social group, that begins to decline over time. In some cases, very quickly.<br /> <br /> Even in cases where Social Rolls are not being used on a short term tactical basis, but going for extended successes in order to win over hearts and minds, there are still going to be limits. No matter how much the jerk Garou insists he has changed his heart and is different now, so let's please please be friends, unless actual behavior changes as well, some of those success aren't going to count, or become reset to zero, or some other modifier.<br /> <br /> It is going to be a very rare person who gets constantly screwed over by a high PB Garou who continues to like them. Most people won't. They might admit the person is charming, or very distinguished, or given any number of social attributes that reflect their high Social dice pool. But they won't actually like them because they know they are toxic.<br /> <br /> At the same time, it is also possible for these kind of jerks to be like Eddie Haskell from the old Leave it Beaver episode. Haskell was a selfish jerk who used people, but he also acted very differently to different people. He was very polite, helpful, and respectful to parents and authority figures, and then acted like a little shit when they weren't around. So such a Garou's reputation might be very different in different social circles.<br /> <br /> If you want to translate this into game mechanics, it is changing the Difficulty from the standard 6 to a higher value - 7,8, 9, or even 10 in certain circumstances - because other people (perhaps only a certain group) now dislike the person intently. And furthermore, even what the jerk Garou is allowed to do in social rolls against people who know what kind of person he is should likely be limited. If that person wants to become designated &quot;leader&quot; for some quest, and the other Garou absolutely won't allow that person to lead them, then no Social Roll can achieve that result. The ST needs to adjudicate the scene so that only a lesser kind of success can be achieved, or at least stagger that it can only be allowed if a minimum number of successes is rolled at high difficulty. And of course, I would always allow someone to simply spend a WP to ignore someone else's mundane social success if they are very opposed to it.<br /> <br /> So I think there are actually some very easy tools for STs to run Pure Breed and not have it lead to absurd conclusions. I think the ST and PCs can probably find some sort of balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:31:02-07:00","id":1124035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123958#post1123958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can play the game however you want but it is a HORROR game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. That doesn't mean PB's mechanical function is actually good for horror, or addressing real world issues like classism. If you're using the game as a metaphor, then the RAW are <b>pro-classism</b> because being a member of the right social classes in Garou society as represented by PB makes you inherently superior. Instead of the rich being rich because they control the sources of power and keep wealth to themselves regardless of merit or contribution to society, Garou live in a world where being born right does actually make you better than other Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, do you know who has the same themes of &quot;Pure Blood&quot; vs &quot;Mud Blood&quot;--FRIGGING HARRY POTTER. </div> </div> </div>Except in Potter-verse, it's bullshit. Pure Blood wizards and witches don't get magical social bonuses for their heritage. The whole reason people call Voldemort Wizard-Hitler is because the bigotry of purity he espouses is supposed to be as stupid poorly founded in realty (and the whole hypocrisy thing).<br /> <br /> Harry Potter would be a very different story if the Pure Bloods were actually right and that wizards born of wizards had inherent magical power that mixed birth wizards didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you dislike Pure Breed as a merit, take note it really just makes a bunch of werewolves into Draco Malfoy. </div> </div> </div>I dislike the way the system handles Pure Breed, not that the concept exists in the game. As noted in my post, I don' advocate removing it, esp. if you include the W20 RAtW rules. I do, however, think that the game would benefit from it being divided into two different traits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123988#post1123988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree because I don't think Social Rolls are as powerful as you seem to describe. There are practical limits in what a Social Roll can accomplish and this can change over time or in different circumstances. Having high social skill is not the same as magical mind control.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent, but I included Gifts in my comments for a reason. Add Persuasion to this (which any social steamroller starting character should have) and having high social skill becomes supernaturally good. And while PB doesn't represent magical mind control, it does get into the issue of supernaturally large dice-pools and what it means to be superhumanly charming even if it's not magical mind whammy stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the beginning, before this truth is actually realized, the person with the big social dice pool is quite successful with getting people to agree with him, do what he wants to do, or simply like him. But over time people begin to learn the truth about this person and begin to feel exploited, ignored, used, or become appalled. </div> </div> </div>And that is the reason a lot of people don't like Pure Breed. You get to keep the bonus dice even if you piss on the ideas that are supposedly the source of them. There's no penalty to Pure Breed's bonus when it rolls out that the ancestors that you're supposed to be living up to would cut your head off if they were still alive because you're behaving so poorly. You bring up a few real life examples, but in real life you've never deal with someone with Charisma 6/Subterfuge 6... so how much can we extrapolate someone tossing 15 dice at you when 10 is supposed to be the peek of human skill?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the &quot;win&quot; is usually just that the other person doesn't know what to say. They can't articulate it in a way that causes them to win the argument because the other person is so skilled at rhetoric. No matter what they say, they'll ultimately feel like an idiot and often begin to simply say nothing at all. But at the same time, they aren't actually convinced by this person - they just don't know how to respond effectively in rhetoric. Even while these people are silent and not disputing the other person (or disputing very poorly), it is obvious they actually are not convinced and are seething in resentment or outrage. In many cases, they are looking around the room or table and hoping someone else, anyone else, will step up and smack the crap out of this guy orally. </div> </div> </div>While W20 is way better than V20 with the social roll rules for things like making sure the difficulty varies based on situation, it doesn't really leave a lot of room for this If a character successfully wins a credibility roll, the target finds them credible. If they get a bunch of successes on an Oratory or Fast-Talk roll, people are going to listen to you. <br /> <br /> It also gets into a real problematic rules situation of, &quot;I want to roll to convince someone, I got more successes than they got to resist/beat the difficulty based on their traits/etc.&quot; and letting people say, &quot;Nah, I'm not convinced anyway.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even in cases where Social Rolls are not being used on a short term tactical basis, but going for extended successes in order to win over hearts and minds, there are still going to be limits. No matter how much the jerk Garou insists he has changed his heart and is different now, so let's please please be friends, unless actual behavior changes as well, some of those success aren't going to count, or become reset to zero, or some other modifier. </div> </div> </div>This is getting into Rule Zero territory to me. I'm not disagreeing with you with how things <b>should be</b> but I don't think the system as is actually represents this. &quot;Purebreed is fine, because I'll just modify the rolls on ST fiat to punish characters abusing it,&quot; isn't really showing PB to be fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:23:21-07:00","id":1124067,"title":"","content":"The thing about social dice is they're not magic, though. They're abstractions to simplify roleplaying.<br /> <br /> It's why Appearance exists.<br /> <br /> If you hate a person with a high social set, it's probably because out of universe, they rolled poorly.<br /> <br /> I often run games without social systems at all just based on character ideas but the idea of Pure Breed is that Garou culture supports it and admires it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T18:12:29-07:00","id":1124105,"title":"","content":"This reminds me of when my friend wanted to run an epic level Forgotten Realms campaign. I chose a Paladin and with enough stuff and boosts and what not got a 32 charisma. The first thing that happened was I had players scream &quot;IF HE STARTS ROLLING TO MAKE ME DO THINGS I QUIT&quot; (...i just wanted to smite well....)<br /> <br /> this leads me to what I've always ruled is that you can't force players to react to social dice unless gifts/disciplines/ect. are involved. I have never met a player who wants to be told &quot;no, you in fact still like that guy&quot;. It never makes for fun role play. I tend to use social dice for NPC's reacting to NPC's and players. This way you can have that smug antagonist who always seems to have friends or influence, and make the players free to react to them how they want. <br /> <br /> I also keep situation in mind. At some point an NPC with a high social pool may have done things that for me, mere social dice are impossible to fix. Kinda like how you can have all the athletics and str you want...you can't fly. You could rule that there just is no dice roll out of this socially. Sure you have gifts like Obligation and Mastery that can force things, but personally I'd rule sometimes gifts like Persuasion and merits just aren't enough. That's just me, and my tables have been rather content with having Pure Breed in the game. It may grant dice, but sometimes dice just aren't enough. Maybe I'm just flexing too much golden rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:02:43-07:00","id":1124122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124067#post1124067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about social dice is they're not magic, though. They're abstractions to simplify roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dice aren't magic. Duh.<br /> <br /> Dice might, however, come from mundane or supernatural sources. PB is supernatural. It's not &quot;I'm just great at ____&quot; like a bunch of social Merits. The book as social traits, with social rules, and social powers, that all interact with each other. The social rules have results that are meant to be followed just like any other roll's results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you hate a person with a high social set, it's probably because out of universe, they rolled poorly. </div> </div> </div>Except key to this whole thing are characters that hate/etc. other characters because they keep rolling well, because they have obnoxiously high dice pools (and easily Merits and Gifts to make them even better). Gnawers don't resent high PB characters using their heritage as a kludge because of bad rolls, but because of good ones. That's why a lot of people don't like how PB works RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I often run games without social systems at all just based on character ideas but the idea of Pure Breed is that Garou culture supports it and admires it. </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't address anything with whether or not the PB mechanics are good. Not running combat didn't change the fact that 1e WtA had a massive rules screw up with damage that made a character with 1 bashing damage impossible to kill, or the pre-errata Revised spirit combat rules making spirits insanely difficult to harm.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the rule zero fallacy thing, is that our ability to work around bad rules doesn't stop them from being bad rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124105#post1124105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this leads me to what I've always ruled is that you can't force players to react to social dice unless gifts/disciplines/ect. are involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally hate this sort of thing. Outside of something like Ex3's Red Rule (which applies to Charms too, not just mundane rules, and is a purely to ensure player comfort and fun over the game going into some of the darker places the setting allows), I don't like players just getting to say, &quot;nope&quot; to roll results unless they have magic to say nope with. The WoD has shitty social mechanics, but it's not hard to implement things like CofD's results from Social Maneuvering where players can accede to the influence attempt's intent, or spend resources to follow the letter but twist the spirit of what they're being influenced to do.<br /> <br /> We don't let players go, &quot;I don't care how the dice fell, I don't want to be hit, so no.&quot; or, &quot;I don't care how the dice fell, I don't lose this chess match.&quot; Expecting players to react to the results of the dice is part of the whole point of using dice to add uncertainty to game play to spurn creative narratives. Just being able to nope out of social rolls shouldn't fly anymore than any other kind of roll.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:23:33-07:00","id":1124128,"title":"","content":"All the dice in the world won't save you from a Difficulty 9 roll.<br /> <br /> If your Pure Breed Whatever Garou constantly screws up, constantly makes a fool of himself, makes lots of bad decisions.. .then he's going to have accumulate penalties to his difficulties for social rolls. Think like the Notoriety flaw; you can have all the renown, all the breeding, but people still think you're a dick. Their instincts tell them to knuckle under, but they still think you're just the absolute worst.<br /> <br /> Adding five dice to a Charisma + leadership roll to convince your sept of a wild, cockamemie plan, after having proved yourself to be a nincompoop, is really just ,more likely to give you botches than anything. If you manage to succeed, and your plan screws up, well, odds are that you will just be shut down by elders next time you pipe up - because rank DOES trump breeding in Garou society. Breeding gives you a chance to make a better impression of yourself, but rank comes with inherent and automatic standing, rights, and benefits.<br /> <br /> And if you mess up bad enough, frequently enough? High breeding doesn't protect you from the Voice of the Jackal. Or the Satire Rite. Or even being thrown out of the tribe.It's also not going ot save your renown - if you are a chronic screw-up, you're just going to be a cliath with esteemed ancestors for a long time while all your peers advance in garou society and gain those legs up on you through the automatic privileges of rank.<br /> <br /> In terms of the play of the game, all Pure Breed really does is give you an advantage in the 'early game.&quot; Eventually the accumulation of renown, experience, Gifts, and Sept status will overshadow and out-perform this background. And it's a mild advantage because, again, it's just bonus dice, and bonus dice are subject to variable difficulties, with larger pools actually ending up a liability at certain thresholds.<br /> <br /> basically, while your sept might fawn over a cub who shows up with Pure Breed for a time, he still has to earn his renown, he still has to earn his status.. .and by the time he does? That Pure Breed is just a mild bonus. Nobody cares that King Albrecht has Pure breed 4, because it is irrelevant - he's a legend with entire sections of the Silver record set aside just for him, with high enough social dice pools to convince you of the wisdom of eating your own arm, paired with a nice dose of Gifts that will adjust that dice pool and difficulty as need be - those four extra dice from Pure Breed don't amount to much on top of all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 08-02-2017, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:26:27-07:00","id":1124129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124122#post1124122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally hate this sort of thing. Outside of something like Ex3's Red Rule (which applies to Charms too, not just mundane rules, and is a purely to ensure player comfort and fun over the game going into some of the darker places the setting allows), I don't like players just getting to say, &quot;nope&quot; to roll results unless they have magic to say nope with. The WoD has shitty social mechanics, but it's not hard to implement things like CofD's results from Social Maneuvering where players can accede to the influence attempt's intent, or spend resources to follow the letter but twist the spirit of what they're being influenced to do.<br /> <br /> We don't let players go, &quot;I don't care how the dice fell, I don't want to be hit, so no.&quot; or, &quot;I don't care how the dice fell, I don't lose this chess match.&quot; Expecting players to react to the results of the dice is part of the whole point of using dice to add uncertainty to game play to spurn creative narratives. Just being able to nope out of social rolls shouldn't fly anymore than any other kind of roll.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand, and respect this but in my 20 years of gaming, I've never met players who wanted to play along those lines, and would quit rather then play along. To sway players it too work socially rping with them instead of rolling dice. Mind you I had a Setite villain who my players did say &quot;I wish I could hate this guy!&quot;. It just took a LOT of work. If I simply rolled Charisma+Expression and rolled well...I would have lost them entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T19:39:41-07:00","id":1124139,"title":"","content":"Social Rules are for other people unless its Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T20:39:22-07:00","id":1124156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124035#post1124035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You bring up a few real life examples, but in real life you've never deal with someone with Charisma 6/Subterfuge 6... so how much can we extrapolate someone tossing 15 dice at you when 10 is supposed to be the peek of human skill?</div> </div> </div> </div>Discrepancies in Dice Pools between characters are discrepancies in dice pools between characters. I don't see what the problem is. That certain characters are capable of feats beyond ordinary human potential is part of the game. That is not infrequent in Werewolf which routinely gives extra bonuses in certain forms, pack totems, and Gifts. When needed, STs adjudicate and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124035#post1124035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is getting into Rule Zero territory to me. I'm not disagreeing with you with how things <b>should be</b> but I don't think the system as is actually represents this. &quot;Purebreed is fine, because I'll just modify the rolls on ST fiat to punish characters abusing it,&quot; isn't really showing PB to be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is so much &quot;Rule Zero&quot; as much as ordinary GMing. It is a normal part of the game for an ST to adjust Difficulty needed, and to say certain actions require a certain number of successes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T21:07:23-07:00","id":1124165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124105#post1124105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me of when my friend wanted to run an epic level Forgotten Realms campaign. I chose a Paladin and with enough stuff and boosts and what not got a 32 charisma. The first thing that happened was I had players scream &quot;IF HE STARTS ROLLING TO MAKE ME DO THINGS I QUIT&quot; (...i just wanted to smite well....)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is always the problem with any kind of social interaction mechanic. Players hate if they feel Player Agency (free will) and the ability to make decisions for themselves is taken away from them. People can tolerate scenes where supernatural mind control (Charm Person, Dominate) impacts a particular scene. They may not like it, but know it is just for that one scene and afterwards they can react as they'd like to. (I also know that some players might be OK with some form of long term mind control that impacts them, but it is usually because they think it makes a good story to RP during, and the PC always needs to buy-in or approve beforehand - they don't like it by ST fiat).<br /> <br /> Usually social mechanics are things PC do to NPCs, and are not things the GM does to the PC or the PCs do to each other precisely because it kills fun. In this regard, Werewolf is no better, but no worse than any other system. It is a problem that RPGs have in general.<br /> <br /> As such, most good GMs seem to fall back on a set of principles on when to employ these mechanics on PCs.<br /> <br /> 1) To establish first impressions.<br /> <br /> 2) To adjudicate immediate reactions that don't negate long term player agency - players are usually fine with being temporarily distracted by flimflam, losing staredowns, being successfully lied to, acknowledging the NPC gave a great speech, song, etc., or even being told they are attracted to someone in some fashion.<br /> <br /> What they don't like is having their control of their own character taken away from them. It doesn't matter WHY (that NPC has Pure Breed, I made my PC's own social skill a dump stat, that NPC has a Merit, that NPC has some other bullshit power that I don't).<br /> <br /> It has been many, many years since I've seen a GM tell a PC what their character believes or must do because of some social mechanic because this is something GMs learn very quickly that PCs hate and will cause players to leave.<br /> <br /> Instead what I see is that PC and GM roleplay out the scene, and only for very specific and immediate reactions are mechanics used when there is some specific conflict that must be resolved, or there is uncertainty on what would happen so it must be left to chance. Regardless of the specific outcome of the encounter, the PC is always free to react or believe whatever they'd like.<br /> <br /> It is perfectly alright for a PC to be told that this person is very charming, commanding, or any other fluff you'd like. But the player will always decide whether they like this person or will follow them.<br /> <br /> Some scenes are harder to adjudicate than the other, but I usually see experienced GMs keep the game fun for the PCs, and inexperienced GMs go through the exact same learning curve regardless of the game they are playing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T21:32:58-07:00","id":1124167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124128#post1124128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the dice in the world won't save you from a Difficulty 9 roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they do.<br /> <br /> 6 dice, difficulty 9, no specialty: 52.68% odds of success, average 0.6 successes.<br /> 10 dice, difficulty 9, specialty: 72.42% odds of success, average 2.0 successes.<br /> 15 dice, difficulty 9, specialty: 80.33% odds of success, average 3.0 successes.<br /> 15 dice, difficulty 7 (-2 from pick a thing), specialty: 96.55% odds of success, average of 6.0 successes.<br /> <br /> More dice is actually better. Your odds of botching don't increase either (just the odds of botches vs. normal failure go up), you're well past that bump in the statistics.<br /> <br /> Oh and you can also spend a WP.<br /> <br /> Even difficulty 10, once you get an applicable specialty, means a buck of dice will still carry you through. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think like the Notoriety flaw; you can have all the renown, all the breeding, but people still think you're a dick. Their instincts tell them to knuckle under, but they still think you're just the absolute worst. </div> </div> </div>The Notoriety Flaw is pretty weak. It's a 3 point Flaw that's -2 dice. Speech Impediment, is only a 1 point Flaw, but a much worse +2 difficulty on verbal communication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adding five dice to a Charisma + leadership roll to convince your sept of a wild, cockamemie plan, after having proved yourself to be a nincompoop, is really just ,more likely to give you botches than anything. </div> </div> </div>Not really. See above math, add in the Oratory rules. Even at diff 9, if you have Persuasion and a bucket of dice, you're most likely to get your Sept killed rather than botch.<br /> <br /> And, again, my point is that the rules make it way too ease to avoid a bad reputation by throwing a bucket of dice at social rolls to avoid blame and negative feelings for the character's dumb actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of the play of the game, all Pure Breed really does is give you an advantage in the 'early game.&quot; Eventually the accumulation of renown, experience, Gifts, and Sept status will overshadow and out-perform this background. </div> </div> </div>Except if the player does it right, they aren't going to suffer significantly in Renown because they'll talk their way out of it, they'll still get XP, so they'll still get Gifts.<br /> <br /> And I mentioned Sept Standing rules as a counter to the mechanical issues with PB in my first post. Though it only applies to your Sept, which means it isn't a solution alone if you're doing a lot of travel in your game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's a mild advantage because, again, it's just bonus dice, and bonus dice are subject to variable difficulties, with larger pools actually ending up a liability at certain thresholds. </div> </div> </div>See above. Though it's strange that you argue about how &quot;minor&quot; +4 dice is, but then you point to Albrecht and having a Gifts to reduce difficulty, which dramatically increase the benefit of more dice. Most of this compounds and the PB dice will continue to provide an edge well into the high XP/Rank area of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124129#post1124129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand, and respect this but in my 20 years of gaming, I've never met players who wanted to play along those lines, and would quit rather then play along.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last clause seems to be a bit... of a goal post shift. The fact that players wouldn't quit over the issue doesn't mean people don't care. Lots of people will play with rules they don't think are great if the play is still fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124156#post1124156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discrepancies in Dice Pools between characters are discrepancies in dice pools between characters. I don't see what the problem is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is equating what someone that you've met in person that's good at seeming nice and getting into a group until people figure out how much of an ass they are doesn't extrapolate well out to superhuman level of traits. You say superhuman stuff is part of the game, but are also arguing that superhumanly good characters aren't really superhumanly good with social stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T21:42:59-07:00","id":1124169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124165#post1124165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is always the problem with any kind of social interaction mechanic. Players hate if they feel Player Agency (free will) and the ability to make decisions for themselves is taken away from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the number of systems over the past 10 or so years that have actually put the effort into making social mechanics that avoid the binary results older games defaulted to, which caused the feeling of lack of player agency. There's plenty of systems around that have social mechanics players actually enjoy even at the risk of their character ending up doing something they didn't want, or having to incorporating a view on an NPC they didn't initially envision.<br /> <br /> People can tolerate mundane social mechanics just fine, when designers put in the effort to make it rewarding to do so.<br /> <br /> The whole set of principles are basically for when you're playing a game that doesn't bother making social mechanics fun to engage with. The WoD is certainly one of those games, but it's certainly not all games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T01:27:55-07:00","id":1124219,"title":"","content":"Rolls can only take you so far until the ST will simply put a stop to it. Just like a high succes in dex+athletics doesn't make you fly, if the sept elders are not going to listen, that is the kibosh to your roll.<br /> <br /> In general as well, it is the STs job to make sure the stat isn't abused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T01:54:20-07:00","id":1124227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1123860#post1123860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, here's how I explained it in my game.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pure Breed is racist and classicist. This is probably the most direct way to explain this and it doesn't reflect well on the Garou. However, there's no real way to dance around this without facing it. The newly turned cub of the Silver Fangs who has never fought a Black Spiral Dancer or cleansed a corrupted caern has pure white fur and blue eyes. You know what that means? Every time he speaks, he will probably be listened to before you. If he beats you up, he'll be believed. If you beat him up, you'll be killed. Why? BECAUSE THE WORLD IS NOT FAIR. Wow, a warrior society based on ancestry and heritage is actually dickish. Who would have thought. It's the World of Darkness, not the world of furry superheroes.</span></i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes.<br /> In a tribal society, I see the Pure Breed trait as something that must be respected.<br /> We are talking about a tribal culture born for war and battle, a society of werewolves that worship Nature,<br /> and Nature is not a peacefully rainbow archetype. Yes. Welcome to reality. She's natural order red in tooth and claws.<br /> The garou are losing a battle, against the world, the wyrm, a lot of humans and an infinite list of enemies.<br /> It's a game of savage horror and desperate war against almost everything.<br /> Yes, they are half human, and it's exactly from the human side, mixed with the urge to mate for survival, that<br /> the Pure Breed must be respected: without it, they risk to loose their memory, what they are, what they fight for.<br /> When I see pure breed oooo silver fang entering the room, even if he's mad, I remember about his ancestor, Igor the Beheader,<br /> who slayed alone an entire pack of black spiral dancers, sending their heads to the baltic ocean, jumping against Kerhn'azag, the<br /> monstrous wyrm dragon from the sea.<br /> That's what happen in my mind when I see a pure breed werewolf. I may think he's a mad silver fang, but I still remember what<br /> is worth to fight for.<br /> Also, that's the world of fu**ing darkness. Not the world of werewolves who want peace and to live in armony with nature. Racism can be a point for the garou.<br /> Most of them despise human society.<br /> Don't make the mistake to think that the human side is the good one, or the wolf side is the good one.<br /> I can't see any other way to depict the garou as ''realistic'', a race that is dying, struggling against everything that moove, fighting for Gaia, meanwhile watching<br /> what is happening to their sacred place, a breed of warrior forged by war and strength thorugh the eras can't be soft.<br /> To survive, they must be strong and merciless.<br /> I can think about a black fury that, if she has time, maybe she is interested in some lgbt movement, and even to fight for them.<br /> Maybe. It's really important this human society problems when you are part of a race of warriors who are losing their holy war against Entrophy itslef and<br /> you are filled with rage, magic and you must breed and fight?<br /> Meh. C'mon.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is of course my view of the world of darkness. Everyone should be free to play as he want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 08-03-2017, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T03:54:46-07:00","id":1124240,"title":"","content":"Basically, Pure Breed is Status except you don't have to do anything for it.<br /> <br /> Is that so bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T04:11:21-07:00","id":1124244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124219#post1124219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rolls can only take you so far until the ST will simply put a stop to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember, everyone saying this, what you're inherently admitting, is that the PB mechanics are bad. If they weren't bad, the ST wouldn't have to put a stop to anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like a high succes in dex+athletics doesn't make you fly, if the sept elders are not going to listen, that is the kibosh to your roll. </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, this is an apples and oranges comparison. &quot;Dex + Athletics doesn't make you fly&quot; because you can't fly (assuming your character can't fly because there are ways!). Elders don't come with the inherent ability to mute people, which means they can understand you, process what you're saying, and even potentially be swayed (unless they have an actual power to avoid this, there are some!). Comparing something that is actually impossible, to something that is only impossible by ST fiat, means you're not comparing the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In general as well, it is the STs job to make sure the stat isn't abused. </div> </div> </div>And it's the system's job to reduce the workload on the ST as much as possible. So if a rule is increasing workload, without sufficient justification for other roles the system has in the game, it should be changed!<br /> <br /> Here a simple house rule to PB (probably needs refinement, I came up with this in a minute):<br /> <br /> If a character with PB takes an action that would earn them negative temporary Renown during a scene, they take a social dice penalty equal to their PB bonus plus the total negative Renown for that action for the remainder of the scene, and PB rating plus half the Renown penalty (round down) until they can make amends for their improper actions. If they rack up multiple negative Renown knocks (as in different actions, if one action qualifies for multiple penalties on the chart, it's one penalty), only use the worst. If subject to a Punishment Rite, the penalty expires when that Rite's duration expires.<br /> <br /> Boom, we don't have to jump through ST fiat hoops. A PB 5 Garou murders another Garou under the false pretense of claiming they're &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; suffer a -26 social dice penalty for the rest of the scene, and -15 dice penalty for a very long time. Your Ancestors and Tribal spirits have turned on you for turning on your heritage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 08-03-2017, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T04:12:27-07:00","id":1124245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124240#post1124240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, Pure Breed is Status except you don't have to do anything for it.<br /> <br /> Is that so bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can't lose it nearly as easily.<br /> <br /> But yes, that is so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T05:29:39-07:00","id":1124255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124245#post1124245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you can't lose it nearly as easily.<br /> <br /> But yes, that is so bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, to each their own. For me, Pure Breed creates a natural kind of enemy. I point out &quot;Arkady&quot; from THE SILVER CROWN if any of you have read it and I recommend you do even though I'm annoyed White Wolf hasn't re-released its books on Kindle. I even talked with David Niall Wilson about trying to find out who we would have to talk to about getting it subcontracted to another publisher. Basically, Arkady is going to be the King of the Garou Nation in North America for the reason he has Pure Breed 5. Albretch has Pure Breed 4 and even then, that is a serious political disadvantage to him. Arkady has killed a Nexus Crawler but that's the kind of thing player characetrs do all the time and he didn't even do it alone. It's all about the fact he's got greater wizarding blood than anyone but the Black and Malfoy families.<br /> <br /> It's a useful storytelling tool.<br /> <br /> It also helps players who shell out for it.<br /> <br /> Would I ever allow it to affect players? No, that's ridiculous, but who does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T06:53:25-07:00","id":1124281,"title":"","content":"If you think that Pure Breed is too powerful in your games, then you should stop prioritizing the social interactions between Garou. If the only social interactions that occur in your games are between Garou, then Pure Breed is going to be overpowered because it effective gives three Attribute dice (+1 Charisma, +1 Manipulation, and +1 Appearance) for the cost of one Background point. However, there is an entire world out there outside of the Garou Nation, and Pure Breed does not help out social interactions with animals, humans, spirits, or other supernatural creatures. If you make it so that Garou-Garou social interactions are 10% or less of the social interactions in your games, you will find that Pure Breed matters a whole lot less (it is one of the reasons why I like the Ahadi and the Beast Courts, the Garou are just one group of many, and Pure Breed just becomes an odd form of status within the Garou ranks).<br /> <br /> I do think that one possible solution though could be to make Pure Breed matter only for social interactions with Garou and Kinfolk of your Tribe. That way, the Tribes without Pure Breed are not excessively disadvantaged, and every character does not feel obligated to take some level of Pure Breed. After all, why should a Bone Gnawer or Wendigo really care if a Silver Fang resembles an Ancestor from 1,000 years ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-03-2017, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T07:21:34-07:00","id":1124288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124165#post1124165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is always the problem with any kind of social interaction mechanic. Players hate if they feel Player Agency (free will) and the ability to make decisions for themselves is taken away from them. People can tolerate scenes where supernatural mind control (Charm Person, Dominate) impacts a particular scene. They may not like it, but know it is just for that one scene and afterwards they can react as they'd like to. (I also know that some players might be OK with some form of long term mind control that impacts them, but it is usually because they think it makes a good story to RP during, and the PC always needs to buy-in or approve beforehand - they don't like it by ST fiat).<br /> <br /> Usually social mechanics are things PC do to NPCs, and are not things the GM does to the PC or the PCs do to each other precisely because it kills fun. In this regard, Werewolf is no better, but no worse than any other system. It is a problem that RPGs have in general.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tell my players &quot;Social actions have consequences&quot; if everyone else thinks someone is awesome and he asked you for a &quot;tiny favor&quot; and you go &quot;FUCK OFF YOU CAN'T TELL ME WHAT TO DO&quot; people are going to treat you exactly like how you'd treat someone who does that IRL. So no I'm not going to make social rolls to tell you what to do, I'm going to make them for how others see the situation.<br /> <br /> This also includes &quot;private&quot; interactions. If Social god man rolls up a bunch of successes and you're completely &quot;FUCK OFF AND DIE HOW DARE YOU TELL ME ANYTHING&quot; he probably has discussions later about how unreasonable you are.<br /> <br /> You end up having harder times getting things from people around the sept, your challenges are more unreasonable, Renown becomes harder to achieve recognition.<br /> <br /> People may not have the experience of being &quot;forced&quot; to do something they don't like by raw charisma but I'm damned sure we've all done things driven by peer pressure we had no desire to do and that's something one can readily relate to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T12:21:39-07:00","id":1124432,"title":"","content":"played werewolf the apocalypse for years now, and never had a problem with pure breed. Honestly, it's one of the least favourite backgrounds among my players, they rather have rage 8 fang daggers and high gnosis to just frenzy and kill any high noble prince with pure breed that wants to tell them what to do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though i don't see why the background should be so problematic... Remember that even pure breed has his limits and renown and roleplay beat pure breed. <br /> Ok, u might be good at social skills and dices but you are surrounded by ready to kill insta warform monster that can easily frenzy even if u trick them and u umiliate them, do u reallly want to end up like meatballs when u try to stop that get of fenrir pack just because u come from a pure breed lineage of silver fang? Good luck with that...<br /> <br /> I remind to u all a little tale from the red talons handbook... do u guys remember how they got their name?<br /> A bold and noble arrogant silver fang (who probably had high pure breed status...).. met a simple and humble red talon:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Those Garou that had chosen to not consort with the humans attended, but since they had no sinuglar alpha, they remained unheeded for much of the debates and during the copilation of the </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Litany\" target=\"_blank\">Litany</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. In the night short before the end of the gathering, a powerful </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ahroun\" target=\"_blank\">Ahroun</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> named </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Fells-Trees?redlink=1&amp;action=edit&amp;flow=create-page-article-redlink\" target=\"_blank\">Fells-Trees</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> stood up and confronted the leading </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Silver_Fang\" target=\"_blank\">Silver Fang</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, asking him what they were supposed to do about the ever-growing population of humans, now that they were no longer allowed to cull them; and why the wolves' vote had not been counted. The Silver Fang answered that he did not know that the wolves were a </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tribe_(WTA)\" target=\"_blank\">tribe</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> and asked him for the name of it. When Fells-Trees pressed on that names were not important, the Fang answered that without a tribal name, the wolves would be considered a pack of marauding scavengers. Angered, Fells-Trees lashed out against the Fang, leaving a bloody swath of claw marks upon his chest. This, Fells-Trees proclaimed, was the name of his tribe and that he would now wait for an answer. From the cuts, the name &quot;Red Talons&quot; was derived, as well as the earliest </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Glyph\" target=\"_blank\">Glyphs</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> used in the Nation.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Guess pure breed couldn't save him that time... remmeber its a game about wild frenzy animals violent and tribal that can leash at u without warning... and u never pet or domesticate a wild wolf.. even with pure breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:05:53-07:00","id":1124491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124281#post1124281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think that Pure Breed is too powerful in your games, then you should stop prioritizing the social interactions between Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize the bonus also applies to all formal challenges, social or not, right? So it still helps in combat and game-craft challenges. It helps in Rank challenges regardless of what you're challenged to do.<br /> <br /> Even if you down play social interactions between Garou (though how, exactly, you do that with the focus on pack and all that is a bit questionable), it's a massive advantage in a hugely important area of Garou Society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124432#post1124432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that even pure breed has his limits and renown and roleplay beat pure breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>How?<br /> <br /> Renown has no mechanical effect. Rank has some impact on challenges, but far less than PB can have. Roleplay swings both ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, u might be good at social skills and dices but you are surrounded by ready to kill insta warform monster that can easily frenzy even if u trick them and u umiliate them, do u reallly want to end up like meatballs when u try to stop that get of fenrir pack just because u come from a pure breed lineage of silver fang? </div> </div> </div>Which is why you use your bucket of social dice to have more allies than they have, so if they attack you, they'll be outnumbered and killed. Also, you know, the most likely to Frenzy characters are the ones that are most likely to have the least combat experience and skill. Higher Rank Garou don't frenzy much (Rank actually matters here!).<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, they ever figure out you're manipulating them, because your bucket of dice makes sure they think you're a good Garou, and anything that goes wrong is someone else's fault for them to vent their Rage on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remind to u all a little tale from the red talons handbook... do u guys remember how they got their name? </div> </div> </div>I also remember all the Red Talon material that says Red Talons are the Tribe most susceptible to following PB blindly, because their lack of experience with human social maneuvering, and not being raised around human cultural ideas of individualism, their instinct to obey for the good of the &quot;pack&quot; overrides any dislike of a leader that hasn't proven themselves weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T16:11:03-07:00","id":1124520,"title":"","content":"The only thing that tends to bug me about Pure Breed (okay not the only thing but that's getting into a discussion outside the narrow mechanical and roleplaying parameters of the topic) is when players portray PCs of tribes that can't take Pure Breed but duck around it by being adoptees from other tribes that have it and take high levels of it anyway. Its not something I'd allow as an ST (at least not as often as I've seen it happen) but its apparently something a lot do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T20:25:07-07:00","id":1124599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem#post1123755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The queen can be the queen all she wants. If she walks up and kicks my dog and slaps my kid. I'm gonna beat her to a pulp. All the noble breeding in the word is not gonna stop that. And will not give her any benefit at all.<br /> <br /> If a pure blood garou of any level, walks up and just breaks their neck, are either of your characters gonna care at all about their lineage? Or will they frenzy and make garou paste. any onlookers too, can't care at all about random murder. so screw the bonus dice to whatever would be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not how pure breed works. Yes, it gives you conspicuous bonuses on social relations, but it's not a mystical cloak of invulnerability. Not even a Rank 5 elder could slay a cub with impunity, and it would sure as hell cost some honour and a trial at least. Pure breed and social standing may help you surviving a trial or get away with less harm than others, but breaking the Litany is going to dock your reputation no matter what.<br /> <br /> Obviously, if you're in the domain of a Silver Fang queen surrounded by her loyal guards then it's a completely different matter, and quite alike to how a Prince rules his city. You're free to rage against her at any time and your near-instantaneous death will teach the others that you don't just fuck with the status quo, but don't be mistaken: what killed you was a difference in power and resources and your inability to realize it, not a five-points background.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They'd prefer for it to be removed from the game. Thoughts on this? It's not the first time I've heard people claim PB is broken, or doesn't make sense. </div> </div> </div>It does make a lot of sense tbf. The Bone Gnawers discriminations, the Silver Fangs leading the garou and the way kinfolks are seen servants and breeding ground are all but aspects of the importance of pure breed in the Garou society. Coupled with the importance of the ancestors (and how the Ancestor background allows you access to ancient knowledge) it's a mystical, heroic heritage that shows how yes, as a matter of fact lineage matters in their society. Removing pure breed from the setting would also remove the justification for a lot of things.<br /> <br /> But yes, it IS an overpowered background and that's really easy to see, it should be reworked (along with Spirit Heritage).<br /> Maybe making a bonus of 1 dice every 2 pure breed, or maybe putting a cap on the usage per chapter, i.e.: you have pure breed 4, so you have 4 bonus dice each game session that you can spend on social rolls against werewolves. Once you rolled all the four of them your boosts are done till the next session.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's worth remembering that it's a game we play to have fun. Not everyone wants to have classist themes shoved down their throats with mechanics, and be told that disliking that makes them not really buying into the &quot;dark&quot; of the game. Human society IRL has plenty of dark issues with classism without certain families being supernaturally awesome at social stuff. </div> </div> </div>This feels more like a matter of personal beliefs and less a matter of rules to change. If you or your friends feel, for any reason, uncomfortable on classism issues by all mean remove them, but there's an heavy difference between house ruling to make a campaign more fun and stating that a specific rule should be removed from the game system because some people is just too sensitive to it. Let's leave any social/political issue outside of these forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I simply rolled Charisma+Expression and rolled well...I would have lost them entirely. </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb, I try to not roll social dice too much and let the players RP both their stats and the situations... rolling instead of having the players argue with npcs is just not fun. But I will impose a roll if they're not correctly roleplaying their stats or position. So, if they bow when my elder Silver Fang npc enters the caern I won't roll, but if they try to speak with insolence I'll ask a contested roll.<br /> Rolls are there to help interpretation, not to replace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T21:06:29-07:00","id":1124606,"title":"","content":"That is one reason why I think that PB should only apply to members of your tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T00:57:40-07:00","id":1124651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124599#post1124599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not how pure breed works. Yes, it gives you conspicuous bonuses on social relations, but it's not a mystical cloak of invulnerability.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point though, is that the bonus persists despite this. It's not, &quot;PB is an automatic get out of jail free card,&quot; but that unless you're kicked out of your Tribe, you never lose those bonuses. Some people (and apparently more common in my gaming circles than the other posters in the thread) find it silly that PB is so mystically potent that you never lose the bonus until you get kicked out of your Tribe.<br /> <br /> The example in the OP might be hyperbolic, but that doesn't mean it isn't a real issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bone Gnawers discriminations, the Silver Fangs leading the garou and the way kinfolks are seen servants and breeding ground are all but aspects of the importance of pure breed in the Garou society. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the concept of PB are really important to this, but the mechanics of PB aren't so much. Gnawers aren't the only Tribe that doesn't get PB, and the Silver Fangs are the only Tribe where you have to take PB. There's plenty of PB 0 characters out there that aren't Gnawers and don't face the discrimination against them for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This feels more like a matter of personal beliefs and less a matter of rules to change. </div> </div> </div>That specific quote is actually far more a matter of personal annoyance at a particular way of talking about the WoD games where the unfairness of the setting is used to defend bad rules because that makes it &quot;dark,&quot; and if you want to fix bad rules you are trying to play &quot;furry superheroes,&quot; for making the game more fair for the players even if the setting is still a shithole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you or your friends feel, for any reason, uncomfortable on classism issues by all mean remove them,... </div> </div> </div>As to this. The problem is not that WtA deals with classism as a topic. The problem is that it says classism (and to an extend ethno-nationalism) is correct by giving bonuses for PB the way it does.<br /> <br /> Let my put it this way. If a game is going to have racism as a topic that is thematically addressed, would you want white characters to have an inherent mechanical advantage over POC characters? If sexism is going to be a topic in the game, do you want character stats to be changed so that sex and gender norms are enforced by the system?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want that. Games that do that aren't seriously addressing the issues. The system is taking a side instead of letting you explore things. If the system says that the &quot;nobles&quot; are inherently mechanically superior to the &quot;commoners&quot; then the system is saying that the nobles are right to assert that they're superior, and the commoners are deluded for thinking that they're not. It doesn't actually let you get into any sort of nuance about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's leave any social/political issue outside of these forums. </div> </div> </div>This is literally impossible. WtA is game that doesn't shy away from social and political issues, so discussing it means those issues are going to have to come up from time to time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:01:57-07:00","id":1124685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124128#post1124128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the dice in the world won't save you from a Difficulty 9 roll.<br /> <br /> Adding five dice to a Charisma + leadership roll to convince your sept of a wild, cockamemie plan, after having proved yourself to be a nincompoop, is really just ,more likely to give you botches than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is factually, genuinely wrong. While sometimes extra dice does increase your risk of botching (1 vs 2 dice at difficulty 10 as an example), it reduces your risk of Failure in ALL situations; it's just that a higher % of the failures that do happen are Botches.<br /> <br /> More dice is ALWAYS good, even at difficulty 9. 8 dice vs 13 dice (good social character with PB 0 vs. good social character with PB 5) means a difference of <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">57.72 / 31.26 / 11.01 (1.8) vs </span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">66.08 / 29.39 / 4.53 (2.4). This means the risk of botching is more than halved, for starters. Furthermore the odds of gaining 1 success or more increases by almost 10%. Your average successes increase by 0.6, which means a lot by aggregate.<br /> <br /> And this is at difficulty 9, the highest difficulty you'll face with most STs. You know what 8 vs. 13 (our Bone Gnawer vs. our Silver Fang with PB 5) dice means at difficulty 6?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">92.06 / 7.61 / 0.33 (3.5)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">97.15 / 2.84 / 0.01 (5.4)</span><br /> <br /> More than a 5% increase in chances to succeed. Chance to fail is reduced by almost 5%, and chance to botch is reduced from nearly a third of a % to almost zero. Average successes are up by 2.<br /> <br /> This is pretty huge, mechanically speaking. It's why Vampire's invest in Celerity 5, even if they don't tend to spend blood on it. It's why Mages have Cults and work together on big spells. Dice make a huge difference at any difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:49:35-07:00","id":1124696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124651#post1124651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point though, is that the bonus persists despite this. It's not, &quot;PB is an automatic get out of jail free card,&quot; but that unless you're kicked out of your Tribe, you never lose those bonuses. Some people (and apparently more common in my gaming circles than the other posters in the thread) find it silly that PB is so mystically potent that you never lose the bonus until you get kicked out of your Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, social battles are more difficult to implement in a game than the physical ones. This particular merit, as I said and really seems that everyone here agrees, is way, way too powerful and should be fixed somehow.<br /> <br /> Let's try suggesting some house rule:<br /> <br /> 1- Pure Breed social dice are usable only once per session (or twice?)<br /> 2- Pure Breed social dice are usable only in a specific field (restricted in the same way specialities are: intimidation, bluffing, charm the masses, etc.)<br /> 3- Pure Breed grants half the social dice (rounded down) but adds some other kind of bonuses, like accessing Sept rank privileges as if the Garou were of higher standing (see &quot;Rage across the world)<br /> 4- Pure Breed doesn't grant social dice at all, but offers a combination of other backgrounds to be tapped once per session (contacts, allies, resources...) in a similar way to the Exalted &quot;Backing&quot; background.<br /> <br /> Don't know, how would you fix this stat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let my put it this way. If a game is going to have racism as a topic that is thematically addressed, would you want white characters to have an inherent mechanical advantage over POC characters? If sexism is going to be a topic in the game, do you want character stats to be changed so that sex and gender norms are enforced by the system?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want that. Games that do that aren't seriously addressing the issues. The system is taking a side instead of letting you explore things. If the system says that the &quot;nobles&quot; are inherently mechanically superior to the &quot;commoners&quot; then the system is saying that the nobles are right to assert that they're superior, and the commoners are deluded for thinking that they're not. It doesn't actually let you get into any sort of nuance about it. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;pure breed&quot; merit is more like when your father was the mayor of your town and everyone knew him. He was a good mayor, too, so now everyone is looking at you and wondering if you're going to be a mayor too when the time comes, and if are you able to be as good as him. And not only your father, but your grandfather, your great-grandfather and his father too were loved mayors of the city.<br /> So yes, as long as you behave like an impartial and caring mayor should, the people will listen to you and believe you more than your rivals. If you screw up, then you're an embarassment and a failure for your family. It may not feel fair in game terms, but social standing can be tied to a family (connections, culture, power, money...) and it gives bonuses to social relations with people that knows the family.<br /> <br /> And everyone in the Garou world knows the family of a Pure Breed.<br /> Still needs better rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:00:11-07:00","id":1124698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124169#post1124169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for the number of systems over the past 10 or so years that have actually put the effort into making social mechanics that avoid the binary results older games defaulted to, which caused the feeling of lack of player agency. There's plenty of systems around that have social mechanics players actually enjoy even at the risk of their character ending up doing something they didn't want, or having to incorporating a view on an NPC they didn't initially envision.<br /> <br /> People can tolerate mundane social mechanics just fine, when designers put in the effort to make it rewarding to do so.<br /> <br /> The whole set of principles are basically for when you're playing a game that doesn't bother making social mechanics fun to engage with. The WoD is certainly one of those games, but it's certainly not all games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read The Succubus Club; Dead Man's Party. Social rolls NEVER rob PCs or NPCs or free will.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> James is a bit of a rogue in his Tribe, and he doesn't like playing in a team. He does, however, want to learn new Gifts, and being in good standing with the Tribe is a big part of that (with many Spirits being more friendly towards those who are working well with their Tribe). John has PB 5 and Charisma 5, and Expression 4. He states in plain view of other members of their Tribe that James has to be more of a team player, otherwise he can't expect help from anyone else when he needs it.<br /> <br /> John rolls his 14 dice against a difficulty of 6 (or 4 if he has a Merit) and gets 6 successes. Others nod in agreement, people avoid making eye contact with James. James COULD storm off and ignore the result of the roll, but he would face social debuffs as a result. NPCs would be very slow to help him, train him etc. Next time James needs help he'll be rolling at +3 difficulty because he is at -3 favour as a result of John's roll.<br /> <br /> So James still has full agency, there are just social problems arising from his behaviour and his failure to comply with John's successful roll. If John were to botch? He looks like a control freak and loses Favour, and James gets to keep his devil-may-care attitude for a while longer.<br /> <br /> If James comes around and becomes a team player as a result, John might be in for an increase in Renown (I don't remember which three things Garou have off the top of my head, Wizdom maybe?) for getting one of his relatives to play their part better. This means social stats can actually be as potent as other stats, situationally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-04-2017, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:03:30-07:00","id":1124699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124288#post1124288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I tell my players &quot;Social actions have consequences&quot; if everyone else thinks someone is awesome and he asked you for a &quot;tiny favor&quot; and you go &quot;FUCK OFF YOU CAN'T TELL ME WHAT TO DO&quot; people are going to treat you exactly like how you'd treat someone who does that IRL. So no I'm not going to make social rolls to tell you what to do, I'm going to make them for how others see the situation.<br /> <br /> This also includes &quot;private&quot; interactions. If Social god man rolls up a bunch of successes and you're completely &quot;FUCK OFF AND DIE HOW DARE YOU TELL ME ANYTHING&quot; he probably has discussions later about how unreasonable you are.<br /> <br /> You end up having harder times getting things from people around the sept, your challenges are more unreasonable, Renown becomes harder to achieve recognition.<br /> <br /> People may not have the experience of being &quot;forced&quot; to do something they don't like by raw charisma but I'm damned sure we've all done things driven by peer pressure we had no desire to do and that's something one can readily relate to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, exactly. You just need mechanics to back this up and I CANNOT RECOMMEND DEAD MAN'S PARTY ENOUGH BUY IT IT'S ON AMAZON OR GET THE PDF JUST DO IT OKAY EVERYONE GRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRR","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:48:52-07:00","id":1124797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124244#post1124244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just remember, everyone saying this, what you're inherently admitting, is that the PB mechanics are bad. If they weren't bad, the ST wouldn't have to put a stop to anything.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, you could easily see any roll as this. Rolling to attack the sept leader, rolling for rites when not fitting,etc.<br /> <br /> As for not losing it when doing bad things, again, who says they don't. Even if the RAW doesn't, so much of the writing and setting information points out how Rank and Renown do still matter more. The ST can say the character lost favour in the eyes of the totem and therefore loses the dice advantage, just as the ST might say the PC can't use a rite or another thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:39:01-07:00","id":1124830,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Pure Breed has to be bought at character creation, which means less points to spend on other traits. So it's not 100% benefit with no tradeoffs.<br /> <br /> Also I suspect some of the complaints about how pure breed works may be coming from players who aren't quite willing to let their characters get imnersed in the setting. We have to remember we are stepping outside ourselves to create a good story, which, in my experience, is even more fun and ultimately more rewarding when my character does something that is obviously wrong to me as a player because it's what he would do. It makes the storytelling experience richer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T11:54:39-07:00","id":1124862,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed represents the way that the greatest heroes of the Garou Nation, it's leaders, wisemen and warriors will be blessed with being able to spiritually pass a portion of their greatness down to their descendants. Of course that doesn't mean their kids or grandkids or great-grandkids will be <i>worthy</i> of that blessing but it's also never seem particularly &quot;racist&quot; or terrible to me, and in fact I am having a hard time wrapping my head around the idea that it is really bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:10:43-07:00","id":1124868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124696#post1124696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, social battles are more difficult to implement in a game than the physical ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not. Again, this is something that's seen plenty of design evolution compared to the core WoD systems from '91. Social &quot;battles&quot; are only difficult if you try to treat them as simple binary checks (not that these don't have their place too), or fail to set the stakes and consequences of social actions in a fashion that is fun to engage with (a lot of &quot;social combat&quot; systems aren't fun because they just turn something like Willpower into your social &quot;health&quot; bar until you get rolled into submitting agency).<br /> <br /> Social mechanics lagged behind physical mechanics in quality of design for a bunch of reasons. But the larger RPG design universe is past that. We have successful games like Cortex Plus Drama where everything is a social roll (all your dice pools are built with Relationships and Values). We have more traditional games incorporating better social mechanics (already referenced the optional rules in Succubus Club for VtM as an example).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This particular merit, as I said and really seems that everyone here agrees, is way, way too powerful and should be fixed somehow. </div> </div> </div>I'm not getting the impression from the thread that most people agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't know, how would you fix this stat? </div> </div> </div>As I've mentioned a few times, I think the biggest issue is that PB is two things that shouldn't be put together, and that shaky foundation is why it's always been a bit of a problem.<br /> <br /> If I were given free hand with the game, I'd divide PB into Heritage (which I'd fold Spirit Heritage into as well to keep things neater), and Authority. Heritage would cover the &quot;physical&quot; aspects of PB such as visual appearance, being good breeding stock, and so on. It can't be taken away, but the social bonuses would be very situational. Authority would be more like PB now where you're mystically blessed with command over other Garou. The drawback for being way more broad than Heritage, is that it would be more brittle, with serious mechanical drawbacks for not living up to that authority, and can be lost completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;pure breed&quot; merit is more like when your father was the mayor of your town and everyone knew him. </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't. This example is pretty much exactly what the Notable Heritage Merit is for. PB is more than this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124797#post1124797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, you could easily see any roll as this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, really. See my counter point to the &quot;No you can't fly&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if the RAW doesn't, so much of the writing and setting information points out how Rank and Renown do still matter more. </div> </div> </div>If the mechanics and the lore are at odds with each other, the mechanics should change to represent what the lore says. If Rank and Renown are supposed to trump PB, they should actually do that in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ST can say the character lost favour in the eyes of the totem and therefore loses the dice advantage, just as the ST might say the PC can't use a rite or another thing. </div> </div> </div>Again, Rule Zero fallacy. &quot;The ST can fix it,&quot; means it's broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124830#post1124830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that Pure Breed has to be bought at character creation, which means less points to spend on other traits. So it's not 100% benefit with no tradeoffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, it's actually a problem in that the creation only Backgrounds are either a bit of a trap (Rites are really useful to have, but you can learn them in-game for free when you find a teacher), or turn into must-buy traits (you can only get some of them at creation, so you're going to focus on those and pick up the others in-play).<br /> <br /> A character that doesn't take PB can never get it later. A character that doesn't take Allies or Contacts can get them for free with RP as the game progresses (and for some such backgrounds, PB can make getting them even easier).<br /> <br /> In most groups the social norms to not go super optimization happy with WoD games constrains this, but that's people pushing back against the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I suspect some of the complaints about how pure breed works may be coming from players who aren't quite willing to let their characters get imnersed in the setting. </div> </div> </div>I think it's kind of a bad rhetorical device to assert the &quot;real&quot; motivations of other people instead of listening to them. They might not be expressing themselves well, but assigning reasons for their complaints that suit your view point isn't really good faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:05:14-07:00","id":1125026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124868#post1124868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're not. Again, this is something that's seen plenty of design evolution compared to the core WoD systems from '91.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's also true for combat rolls, and as much as I like the Storyteller system I can't not notice how long a fight lasts. Roll attack, roll dodge, roll damage, roll soak, wait for your opponent to do the same, now do that again for extra attacks. The thing I like the most is how every point matters (something that doesn't happen with several d6 systems and all the d20), the easiness of calculations and how, it still needs to speed up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I were given free hand with the game, I'd divide PB into Heritage (which I'd fold Spirit Heritage into as well to keep things neater), and Authority. Heritage would cover the &quot;physical&quot; aspects of PB such as visual appearance, being good breeding stock, and so on. It can't be taken away, but the social bonuses would be very situational. Authority would be more like PB now where you're mystically blessed with command over other Garou. The drawback for being way more broad than Heritage, is that it would be more brittle, with serious mechanical drawbacks for not living up to that authority, and can be lost completely. </div> </div> </div>If PB lacks of something is brittleness, since no thing could ever make it go away except being cast out from your tribe (and that never happens).<br /> But implement harsher penalities to renown for pure breeders is a nice idea even for current campaigns. Got PB 4 and run away from a fight? Please lose these 3 glory points instead of just one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Spirit Heritage is still as broken as pure breed, especially for a Theurge. Its only saving grace is the chance to make enemies of the spirit brood appear, but I'd rework it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While true, it's actually a problem in that the creation only Backgrounds are either a bit of a trap (Rites are really useful to have, but you can learn them in-game for free when you find a teacher), or turn into must-buy traits (you can only get some of them at creation, so you're going to focus on those and pick up the others in-play). </div> </div> </div>Rites require time to be learnt, and a favour to be done to the one teaching them. You won't usually have a whole week to spend learning your level one rite once the story begins, and you may have to travel away from your master to follow whatever you need to. One point in Rites means that you and your pack don't get naked in the Umbra or after shifting. Don't spend it and you may face 10-12 sessions before the storyteller actually gives you some pause to take your course.<br /> And that's a first level rite, how many sessions would you need to learn descent in the underworld?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character that doesn't take PB can never get it later. A character that doesn't take Allies or Contacts can get them for free with RP as the game progresses (and for some such backgrounds, PB can make getting them even easier). </div> </div> </div>You just don't get contacts for free, you have to work to get them and you can't really choose who's going to need your help and who will owe you favours. Add this to the fact that the Curse makes really, really hard for you to earn humans' trust. So, I wouldn't really talk about contacts, allies or resources as &quot;wasted&quot; background points, since it's unlikely that a storyeller is going to leave your character enough time to find and keep a day job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:41:54-07:00","id":1125043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124868#post1124868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, it's actually a problem in that the creation only Backgrounds are either a bit of a trap (Rites are really useful to have, but you can learn them in-game for free when you find a teacher), or turn into must-buy traits (you can only get some of them at creation, so you're going to focus on those and pick up the others in-play).<br /> <br /> A character that doesn't take PB can never get it later. A character that doesn't take Allies or Contacts can get them for free with RP as the game progresses (and for some such backgrounds, PB can make getting them even easier).<br /> <br /> In most groups the social norms to not go super optimization happy with WoD games constrains this, but that's people pushing back against the game.<br /> <br /> I think it's kind of a bad rhetorical device to assert the &quot;real&quot; motivations of other people instead of listening to them. They might not be expressing themselves well, but assigning reasons for their complaints that suit your view point isn't really good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to express my opinion mildly by using phrases like &quot;I suspect ... some complaints ... may be coming ...&quot; to avoid seeming like I was &quot;asserting the real motivations of other people,&quot; but apparently that didn't come across. I could be totally wrong, and I'll readily admit that my bad past experiences with power-gamers, aka people who &quot;go super optimization happy,&quot; tends to make me see them where they aren't. Also -- and this is coming from someone who doesn't have an intimidating or aggressive bone in his body -- we're using a forum where everyone is free to reply and say &quot;your suspicion doesn't apply to me&quot; in his or her own voice, without any need for hurt feelings on either end. If it makes you feel any better, my suspicion wasn't aimed at anyone in particular, and not at all at you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For whatever it may be worth, I'll make a second try to express myself. I get the impression that some people don't like Pure Breed because it's a real, natural advantage that can't be duplicated or undermined by creative optimization of characters who don't have it. For my part, I don't have a problem with the Pure Breed background, and I don't have a problem with my character, who has no pure breed at all, being affected by it, but maybe that's because I haven't yet seen it abused, and when I do, I'll come to dislike it.<br /> \u200b<br /> A relevant counter-argument to your particular position is that I think a mechanical advantage for a certain human race, or a certain sex, is a false analogy, because Pure Breed is a fictional, spiritual, Garou trait, and not one that we encounter in the real world. Is it not plausible to meet a Get of Fenris who's descended from European aristocracy, whose family is still rich and powerful in the human world, but who happened not to inherit the Pure Breed trait as a Garou? He'd still be treated as an influential person in human society, but there would be no in-game mechanical advantage to his nobility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T02:15:21-07:00","id":1125144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125026#post1125026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, Spirit Heritage is still as broken as pure breed, especially for a Theurge. Its only saving grace is the chance to make enemies of the spirit brood appear, but I'd rework it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Spirit Heritage isn't as broken as PB on the simply grounds that it only applies to a specific type of spirit, where PB works on all Garou (PB works if you're rolling against BSDs). Spirit Heritage's RAW spirit groups are probably too broad, but at least - as you note - it has a bit more built in RP hooks going for it as the spirits your connected to are going to want to involve you in their stuff, which can pull you away from your Garou duties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rites require time to be learnt, and a favour to be done to the one teaching them. You won't usually have a whole week to spend learning your level one rite once the story begins, and you may have to travel away from your master to follow whatever you need to. One point in Rites means that you and your pack don't get naked in the Umbra or after shifting. Don't spend it and you may face 10-12 sessions before the storyteller actually gives you some pause to take your course.<br /> And that's a first level rite, how many sessions would you need to learn descent in the underworld? </div> </div> </div>The rules for learning Rites are kinda dumb, (though the roll and its difficulty is worse than this) in that they use real world time frames instead of narrative time So how much sting the learning times have varies wildly by group/playstyle.<br /> <br /> Yeah, if your group tends to have 10-12 sessions before there's any down time, Rite acquisition is going to be slow (though how long the down time is will matter too). If a group tends towards 3-4 sessions before downtime, it'll be a lot faster.<br /> <br /> But the point is still that learning Rites is something that is fairly accessible in play. Learning Rites are also good story hooks for smaller side things as you have to find teachers, who might want some payment for teaching you, so that generates more story and more stuff to enjoy. It's not just a cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just don't get contacts for free, you have to work to get them and you can't really choose who's going to need your help and who will owe you favours. Add this to the fact that the Curse makes really, really hard for you to earn humans' trust. So, I wouldn't really talk about contacts, allies or resources as &quot;wasted&quot; background points, since it's unlikely that a storyeller is going to leave your character enough time to find and keep a day job. </div> </div> </div>I did say, &quot;with RP.&quot; And as it relates back to PB, you use PB to build up influence in Garou society, grow things like Mentor and Kinfolk, and then use those to help gain/maintain Backgrounds that require more human interactions so things like the Curse aren't as bad. You can't go in the other direction to get more PB.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125043#post1125043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A relevant counter-argument to your particular position is that I think a mechanical advantage for a certain human race, or a certain sex, is a false analogy, because Pure Breed is a fictional, spiritual, Garou trait, and not one that we encounter in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make it a false analogy though. Analogies, by their nature, involve comparing things that aren't the same, so there are bound to be differences. An analogy is false when the differences invalidate the core comparison.<br /> <br /> How does PB being a purely fictional trait invalidate the comparison the RPG abstractions of real traits? I might have never encountered PB IRL, but I've absolutely encountered people that believe in racial purity, and directly espoused a form of it where they're the superior ones, and I'm in the inferior category. So despite the fictional aspect of PB, it's not so outside human experience that the comparisons don't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it not plausible to meet a Get of Fenris who's descended from European aristocracy, whose family is still rich and powerful in the human world, but who happened not to inherit the Pure Breed trait as a Garou? He'd still be treated as an influential person in human society, but there would be no in-game mechanical advantage to his nobility. </div> </div> </div>Well.. that's what the Notable Heritage Merit is for? If you want a werewolf that has a heritage in the human world that provides a mechanical benefit, there's a Merit for that. So yes, a Fenrir that doesn't have PB but does have some sway from their human ancestry is completely something the system models.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T03:44:43-07:00","id":1125163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124862#post1124862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed represents the way that the greatest heroes of the Garou Nation, it's leaders, wisemen and warriors will be blessed with being able to spiritually pass a portion of their greatness down to their descendants. Of course that doesn't mean their kids or grandkids or great-grandkids will be <i>worthy</i> of that blessing but it's also never seem particularly &quot;racist&quot; or terrible to me, and in fact I am having a hard time wrapping my head around the idea that it is really bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in simple terms it's because it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed doesn't mean you're great.<br /> <br /> Look at Arkady, a man willing to sell his fellows down the road to the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> It just means you LOOK the part of being a badass hero of legend.<br /> <br /> It's essentially a very specific kind of cheap Appearance bonus like the Primal Urge merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-05-2017, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:37:22-07:00","id":1125239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125163#post1125163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just means you LOOK the part of being a badass hero of legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Liked your comment, BUT I'd argue that this is intentional. You Seem like a Garou of Destiny, like the perfect leader, but it's just a sort of spiritual hangover from your truly great ancestors. Werewolves don't really seem to understand that it is their constant adherence to *tradition* that often leads to their downfall; a sort of pseudo-nepotism is very fitting.<br /> <br /> Basically PB means &quot;look, Garou are so pathologically obsessed with their heritage that just being descended from someone great can make you very appealing (on a supernatural level) to other Garou...&quot;<br /> <br /> I would, however, introduce a 1 point Merit which means that Pure Breed doesn't effect you; you simply have beliefs that contradict the concept heavily enough that the mystical background has no effect on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:46:52-07:00","id":1125243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125239#post1125239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Liked your comment, BUT I'd argue that this is intentional. You Seem like a Garou of Destiny, like the perfect leader, but it's just a sort of spiritual hangover from your truly great ancestors. Werewolves don't really seem to understand that it is their constant adherence to *tradition* that often leads to their downfall; a sort of pseudo-nepotism is very fitting.<br /> <br /> Basically PB means &quot;look, Garou are so pathologically obsessed with their heritage that just being descended from someone great can make you very appealing (on a supernatural level) to other Garou...&quot;<br /> <br /> I would, however, introduce a 1 point Merit which means that Pure Breed doesn't effect you; you simply have beliefs that contradict the concept heavily enough that the mystical background has no effect on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Glad you liked it.<br /> <br /> I think I may have less issue with this because I think of the rule here as an abstraction while others (not you specifically) are taking it a bit more literal. It's actually WHY I dislike the idea of Pure Breed as a purely spiritual phenomenon and wish it was just, &quot;You look like someone's stereotypical idea of a Get of Fenris [Charlie Hunam], Black Fury [Gal Godot], or Bone Gnawer [There is none.]&quot;<br /> <br /> I would never give Pure Breed any magical powers over a player character.<br /> <br /> Instead, like appearance, it's just something which works in the background noise of MOST Garou. Like, say, appearance. I am, for example, attracted to Sherilyn Fenn as my go-to movie star crush and generally like black haired pale-skinned women ala Lucita (fictional) and Hayley Atwell (not fictional). They get a hypothetical bonus when dealing with me. I generally won't be upset with beautiful people who don't look like that but I have a &quot;type.&quot; In the honor obsessed culture of the Garou where lineage, tradition, reincarnation (until it was retconned away) and so on are so important--most Garou are always looking for some sign of the past or what a Garou is SUPPOSED TO BE LIKE.<br /> <br /> However, were it important for a character that is passionately hateful about Pure Bred werewolves like a Bone Gnawer serial killer who hunts--obviously, it won't give you any bonus against them.<br /> <br /> Rules in RPGs should be flexible versus story, especially in the Storyteller Games.<br /> <br /> Evan Heals the Past actually is a good example of how this could work in a game even if he's ironically supposed to be Pure Bred. Evan is a Caucasian kid from suburbia who does not have any Native American appearance let alone culture. He is, in simple terms, Wendigo Pure Breed 0. Someone who looked much more like Tecumseh and radiates that kind of &quot;Wendigo stoic barely simmering anger&quot; would have a Pure Bred 5.<br /> <br /> Arguably this means Pure Breed should mostly be tribal and I can't help but think Bone Gnawers WOULDN'T take it that seriously but Vampire Status works on Anarchs so that's just how the rules go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T18:20:32-07:00","id":1125435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125243#post1125243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks! Glad you liked it.<br /> <br /> I think I may have less issue with this because I think of the rule here as an abstraction while others (not you specifically) are taking it a bit more literal. It's actually WHY I dislike the idea of Pure Breed as a purely spiritual phenomenon and wish it was just, &quot;You look like someone's stereotypical idea of a Get of Fenris [Charlie Hunam], Black Fury [Gal Godot], or Bone Gnawer [There is none.]&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: Effects on human appearance and human ethnic requirements got chucked in W20 exactly for this reason. It only affects the appearance of your wolf forms, at least unless ParaWolf does something very, very ill-advised in W:tA 5th...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would never give Pure Breed any magical powers over a player character </div> </div> </div>Social influence isn't a form of magical power unless it comes from magic. This doesn't quite qualify like Persuasion would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Evan Heals the Past actually is a good example of how this could work in a game even if he's ironically supposed to be Pure Bred. Evan is a Caucasian kid from suburbia who does not have any Native American appearance let alone culture. He is, in simple terms, Wendigo Pure Breed 0. Someone who looked much more like Tecumseh and radiates that kind of &quot;Wendigo stoic barely simmering anger&quot; would have a Pure Bred 5. </div> </div> </div>There's a mountain of problems involving native identity and its denial based on stereotypical features here. That aside, as a reminder, PB doesn't influence your Homid features or require an ethnic background (though Wendigo isn't looking for recruits among pale European descendants, so no one is getting their foot in the door there, unlike with the Uktena), so Evan's score of 2 dots from Warriors of the Apocalypse still flies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arguably this means Pure Breed should mostly be tribal and I can't help but think Bone Gnawers WOULDN'T take it that seriously but Vampire Status works on Anarchs so that's just how the rules go. </div> </div> </div>They don't have a pecking order among their own because, as they say, no one is lower (an excuse/irreverent joke used by Gnawers to skirt by the &quot;Respect All Those Beneath Ye&quot; tenet of the Litany), though to note, the Glass Walkers are in the same boat there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T18:22:48-07:00","id":1125436,"title":"","content":"Before we continue, I should clarify I play Pure Breed as MONUMENTALLY PROBLEMATIC. It's just something I play as problematic in a way which creates interesting social interactions and paradoxes. It's a little more iffy than Vampire where everything in their caste system is related to fictional clans, generation, and bloodlines while the Garou are linked to real-life Ethnic Groups.<br /> <br /> However, I think that it offers some interesting dynamics to play off of.<br /> <br /> Especially when you acknowledge it's just a quirk of Garou society. A harmful one no less.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:09:55-07:00","id":1125648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124167#post1124167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure they do.<br /> <br /> 6 dice, difficulty 9, no specialty: 52.68% odds of success, average 0.6 successes.<br /> 10 dice, difficulty 9, specialty: 72.42% odds of success, average 2.0 successes.<br /> 15 dice, difficulty 9, specialty: 80.33% odds of success, average 3.0 successes.<br /> 15 dice, difficulty 7 (-2 from pick a thing), specialty: 96.55% odds of success, average of 6.0 successes.<br /> <br /> More dice is actually better. Your odds of botching don't increase either (just the odds of botches vs. normal failure go up), you're well past that bump in the statistics.<br /> <br /> Oh and you can also spend a WP.<br /> <br /> Even difficulty 10, once you get an applicable specialty, means a buck of dice will still carry you through.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Probability <span style=\"color:#222222\">\u2260 guarantee. Not counting for bad dice, each roll is random. There's also the factor of 1's sucking away successes, the frequent need for multiple successes, and everyone's favorite, the contested roll. And of course, the fact that for most actions in the game, ten successes is the same as five successes - and the difference between three successes and five successes' outcomes i pretty marginal</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Notoriety Flaw is pretty weak. It's a 3 point Flaw that's -2 dice. Speech Impediment, is only a 1 point Flaw, but a much worse +2 difficulty on verbal communication. </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought Notoriety was a difficulty modifier - specific instance aside, you get my point though, how difficulty manipulation has a much higher impact than dice pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. See above math, add in the Oratory rules. Even at diff 9, if you have Persuasion and a bucket of dice, you're most likely to get your Sept killed rather than botch.<br /> <br /> And, again, my point is that the rules make it way too ease to avoid a bad reputation by throwing a bucket of dice at social rolls to avoid blame and negative feelings for the character's dumb actions. </div> </div> </div>Charisma 5, Performance 5, specialty reed instruments, ability aptitude merit, some difficulty-manipulating bonus-dice-giving Gifts active, and a Willpower spent. Congratulations, you have ten successes on your first performance roll. Since performance is an extended roll, you keep going! Nineteen successes, twenty-eight, thirty-eight, you're hot, baby!<br /> <br /> But you're playing a kazoo rendition of Jessica Black's &quot;Friday&quot; in the middle of a Silver Fang moot.<br /> <br /> What happens? Well, in your purely dice-arbitrated system, Falcon himself names you his avatar on earth and you completely change the moot structure of the Silver Fangs - and Garou as a whole -forever. The litany is replaced with the lyrics to that song, and centuries of debate and conflict wrack the garou as a heretical faction tries to play it on the klezmer instead of the holy kazoo.<br /> <br /> However in the actual game that this is taking place in, someone punches you in the face, you choke on it like the harmonica guy from <i>Cabin Fever </i>and the moot goes on with no significant change for your interruption. Because the storyteller is not a dice-arbitrated system. The dice are a supplementary system meant to give the actual arbiter - the storyteller - a guide on how events transpire when chance is a factor. Outside of a comedy-themed game, there is just no chance that a kazoo-weilding galliard is going to traipse around the Crescent Moon caern, adding bad American pop to a recitation of the Silver record. it doesn't happen, regardless of his dice pool, or his difficulty modifiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except if the player does it right, they aren't going to suffer significantly in Renown because they'll talk their way out of it, they'll still get XP, so they'll still get Gifts. </div> </div> </div>Renown explicitly doesn't work that way, for exactly that reason. Yes the semi-mystical nature of renown is a woo-woo handwavey solution to turn an OOC tracking device into an IC construct, but it is what it is. Again this is not a hardcore simulationist game, so you have to allow leeway for these things.<br /> <br /> If you allow PC's to talk their way out of renown loss at your table, do you allow them to talk their way into renown gain with equal ease? In either case, I would extend that the problem isn't the system, but the way you are using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above. Though it's strange that you argue about how &quot;minor&quot; +4 dice is, but then you point to Albrecht and having a Gifts to reduce difficulty, which dramatically increase the benefit of more dice. Most of this compounds and the PB dice will continue to provide an edge well into the high XP/Rank area of the game. </div> </div> </div>After a point, it's needless overkill. Albrecht has so much on his plate that if you were to subtract four dice from his pool, it would make little to no impact on the outcome of his efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:18:39-07:00","id":1125652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1124868#post1124868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, Rule Zero fallacy. &quot;The ST can fix it,&quot; means it's broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it means you're playing a tabletop RPG with human players collaborating to create a story, instead of an automated system using number-strings and hard coding to determine an outcome like an MMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:45:41-07:00","id":1125656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125648#post1125648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However in the actual game that this is taking place in, someone punches you in the face, you choke on it like the harmonica guy from <i>Cabin Fever </i>and the moot goes on with no significant change for your interruption. Because the storyteller is not a dice-arbitrated system. The dice are a supplementary system meant to give the actual arbiter - the storyteller - a guide on how events transpire when chance is a factor. Outside of a comedy-themed game, there is just no chance that a kazoo-weilding galliard is going to traipse around the Crescent Moon caern, adding bad American pop to a recitation of the Silver record. it doesn't happen, regardless of his dice pool, or his difficulty modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that you're not the only one to have pure breed or maximized traits. At the very least half of the Silver Fangs and 1/4 of the shadow lords are going to outclass you.<br /> Also, dice are there to be rolled when there's a reason to, not anytime a player makes an action. And dice rolls should be used to determine who's the winner in a specific situation, not as substitution of roleplay. This is not <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0767.html\" target=\"_blank\"><a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0767.html\" target=\"_blank\">the order of the stick</a>.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except if the player does it right, they aren't going to suffer significantly in Renown because they'll talk their way out of it, they'll still get XP, so they'll still get Gifts. </div> </div> </div>No, renown does not work that way at all. They break a promise, they lose 4 honour no matter the shit they may say to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:51:17-07:00","id":1125657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125652#post1125652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it means you're playing a tabletop RPG with human players collaborating to create a story, instead of an automated system using number-strings and hard coding to determine an outcome like an MMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it gets in the way of the story on a regular basis, it's an edge that might need to get sanded down just a little. After all, the system is there to help, and if it can't, well then...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ILVfzx5Pe-A\" data-code=\"ILVfzx5Pe-A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ILVfzx5Pe-A/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T01:25:53-07:00","id":1125818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125648#post1125648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probability\u2260 guarantee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, really?<br /> <br /> So why did you bring it up in the first place when you made false claims about the probabilities of the dice mechanics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also the factor of 1's sucking away successes, the frequent need for multiple successes, and everyone's favorite, the contested roll. </div> </div> </div>1s cancelling successes were factoring into my numbers, if I removed those... they'd be a lot higher.<br /> <br /> I included the average successes for both addressing the need for multiple successes and contested rolls, to show that more dice does in fact help with both even at difficulty 9 despite your claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course, the fact that for most actions in the game, ten successes is the same as five successes - and the difference between three successes and five successes' outcomes i pretty marginal </div> </div> </div>The game doesn't care about 6+ successes on most rolls. The game has guidelines for the difference between 3 and 5 successes on a roll without specific margins of success. 3 successes is supposed to be a complete success the fully addresses the task, while 5 successes is supposed come with a significant advantage above simply completing the task.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you're playing a kazoo rendition of Jessica Black's &quot;Friday&quot; in the middle of a Silver Fang moot. </div> </div> </div>Your strawman is noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Renown explicitly doesn't work that way, for exactly that reason. Yes the semi-mystical nature of renown is a woo-woo handwavey solution to turn an OOC tracking device into an IC construct, but it is what it is. Again this is not a hardcore simulationist game, so you have to allow leeway for these things. </div> </div> </div>Please try to pay attention to what I said. I didn't say social rolls can completely negate Renown knocks, I said they can get you out of a significant portion of them. For example, you can't suffer the penalties of a Punishment Rite if you convince everyone you don't deserve it. You can offset a small knock with things like maintaining a good relationship with the local kin, since that can be done with good social skills, and winning formal challenges with your bonus dice (which incidentally can cost other people Renown depending on type).<br /> <br /> There's also nebulous things like, do you lose Renown for breaking a rule, if your superiors don't consider you to have broken any rules? Are the spirits going to knock your Renown for questioning your superiors in a possible time of war if your superiors don't feel the questioning was inappropriate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In either case, I would extend that the problem isn't the system, but the way you are using it. </div> </div> </div>No there's a pretty significant issue with the Sample Renown Awards chart and how it works out in play, because it allows for all sorts of ways to cheese the Renown system without the ST stepping in and making it work despite itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After a point, it's needless overkill. Albrecht has so much on his plate that if you were to subtract four dice from his pool, it would make little to no impact on the outcome of his efforts. </div> </div> </div>Weren't you just going on about things like high difficulty, or Contested rolls... in which every edge actually matters? Or have you not looked at his official sheet which... isn't actually that good. His only high end social pool without PB is Charisma + Leadership, and he has zero social oriented Gifts.<br /> <br /> Of course the official sheets for the NPCs are notoriously off base for what PCs tend to achieve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125652#post1125652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it means you're playing a tabletop RPG with human players collaborating to create a story, instead of an automated system using number-strings and hard coding to determine an outcome like an MMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the fact that you clearly need to look up what the Rule Zero fallacy is, the fact that RPGs have humans running them doesn't justify bad rules. We have humans running the games because the rules will never be perfect, but that's not an excuse to not fix rules that are broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125656#post1125656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that you're not the only one to have pure breed or maximized traits. At the very least half of the Silver Fangs and 1/4 of the shadow lords are going to outclass you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, dice are there to be rolled when there's a reason to, not anytime a player makes an action. And dice rolls should be used to determine who's the winner in a specific situation, not as substitution of roleplay. </div> </div> </div>And roleplay shouldn't ignore traits even if you don't roll them. A character with a 15 dice pool vs. a character with a 6 dice pool should be roleplayed in a fashion that respects how massively outclassed the second character is, even if you opt not to roll things.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not going to let you roll, because if you rolled you'd probably win,&quot; isn't actually caring about roleplay, nor is it really honoring not rolling for the sake of expedience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, renown does not work that way at all. They break a promise, they lose 4 honour no matter the shit they may say to others. </div> </div> </div>See above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T03:03:12-07:00","id":1125833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125818#post1125818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention that you're not the only one to have pure breed or maximized traits. At the very least half of the Silver Fangs and 1/4 of the shadow lords are going to outclass you. </div> </div> </div>Citation please.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need citations on the presence of pure breed or social traits in the Silver Fangs? Have you ever read a manual? =p<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And roleplay shouldn't ignore traits even if you don't roll them. A character with a 15 dice pool vs. a character with a 6 dice pool should be roleplayed in a fashion that respects how massively outclassed the second character is, even if you opt not to roll things.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not going to let you roll, because if you rolled you'd probably win,&quot; isn't actually caring about roleplay, nor is it really honoring not rolling for the sake of expedience. </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point entirely. The line here is &quot;I'm not going to let you roll persuasion unless you find reasons good enough to persuade the elders&quot;. Let's see a short exemple of &quot;Friday vs Moot&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#008000\">Good:</span></b><br /> Storyteller: &quot;The elders approach you, and the Warden raises his claw to strike you&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;I show him the palms in a stop gesture, and beg him to spare my life&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;The Warden snarls and asks why should they be merciful on someone that doesn't seem able to respect the traditions or even the spirits&quot;<br /> P: &quot;I tell him that they seemed to take too seriously the chants and rites, and that I felt the necessity to remind them to look for meaning in the nature of our bond with the Caern spirits more than in the words. After all, isn't it the role of us Ragabash?&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Another elder looks at you and says &quot;Yet spirits are a serious matter, and to disrespect them this way does not bode well for either us or the Caern. Your so-called lesson was poorly built, and possibly dangerous if you attempted it to a Moot hold by a sept different than your own&quot;&quot;<br /> P: &quot;I apologise for being so improper. It didn't realize it was such a grave offense. But I'm young and I still have much to learn&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Okay, roll persuasion. Lose two wisdom too.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Bad:</span></b><br /> Storyteller: &quot;The elders approach you, and the Warden raises his claw to strike you&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;I roll persuasion to convince them to not harm me&quot;<br /> Storyteller: &quot;Okay, roll away&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Is the difference clear enough?<br /> The point is not to forbid a roll that your player are going to win, is to have players earn their roll through roleplaying. Otherwise it's just a dice game and no different from the strip I previously linked. If they can't find a motive sensible enough to be considered by the elders they should just not have a roll: dice are a mean to solve those actions you can't say for sure how they should go, not magic. If a player splats after a 200 meters drop you roll neither for damage nor soak, he's just dead.<br /> <br /> Also, only because they roll 15 dice versus 6 it doesn't mean that the statistics are in their favour, since you still need to take the action modifiers into account. In the infamous case of Friday vs Moot, the defender will roll 6 dice at difficulty 4 while the upstart pop singer is going to have, don't know, difficulty 10? To mitigate the elders enough to not punish him officially, if he actually want to make them praise him it's going to be a threshold 5 too (aka: to have his first success he needs to roll 5 successes).<br /> He might not even reach the social part at all, to be fair, if the GM chooses to roll frenzy for the elders before the player gets a chance to speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See above. </div> </div> </div>Seen and no, the renown is not only a ranking system inside the garou society but also a marker of the consideration you have among the spirits (and Gaia). You earn most of your renown questing around, away from your elders, so if things were as you're theorizing the Garou should:<br /> <br /> 1) earn Renown points only at the moots<br /> 2) earn Renown points only based on what you tell at the moots. So, if you have a pack of coward and lying piece of shits you should be able to omit every time you fled from the enemy, or that you broke your word, or freed banes. A philodox can only detect lies, so if you stick with omissions you will never lose a single point of renown. It is so convenient, why isn't it done by every Garou? It would also help to fight for Gaia, since this net of lies also means that everyone will reach rank 5 faster this way.<br /> <br /> But that's not how it happens. Somehow Gaia just knows, and maybe some peeking spirit too. Feel free to use social rolls as a renown shield for your characters if that suits your campaign, but it's really not how the Renown system was intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 08-07-2017, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T04:34:59-07:00","id":1125842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125833#post1125833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need citations on the presence of pure breed or social traits in the Silver Fangs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need citations that 50% of Silver Fangs and 25% of Shadowlords are automatically going to outclass a given character socially, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you ever read a manual? </div> </div> </div>Strange from someone that's saying one thing, and then shifting the goalposts to try to claim otherwise. Also strange for someone that's rather misrepresenting what I've said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The line here is &quot;I'm not going to let you roll persuasion unless you find reasons good enough to persuade the elders&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That's no the line quite a few people have expressed here. As well, this attitude is extremely annoying because it forces social character players to be at least as good as their characters. Players aren't always up to acting their way through everything. &quot;My character should know the right thing to say, because they've got all the stats, but I'm having a brain fart,&quot; shouldn't be punished with, &quot;then you don't get to roll you horrible player!&quot; Because that's not fun, and this is a game. You don't hold back attack rolls because the player doesn't pick the right stance and attack direction to best strike around the opponents defenses. You just let them roll the attack. Same deal here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the difference clear enough? </div> </div> </div>Nope, because your example is, basically, an idiotic, &quot;roll-playing vs role-playing&quot; argument that has nothing to do with anything that matters; like 99.99% of all &quot;role-play not roll-play!&quot; themed statements.<br /> <br /> Unless you're attempting to argue that people that can optimize builds and cheese the system are incapable of role-playing, this example communicates nothing of value to the discussion of the PB background's mechanics or logic.<br /> <br /> And the &quot;Friday vs. Moot&quot; example is bullshit, and that did nothing to salvage it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is not to forbid a roll that your player are going to win, is to have players earn their roll through roleplaying. </div> </div> </div>Except a large number of people have argued that PB's mechanics are fine, because the ST can just stop the abuse 'as needed' in play, not because of this whole &quot;earn your roll&quot; nonsense.<br /> <br /> As well, players don't have to &quot;earn their roll.&quot; The rolls are there to abstract a situation where success, failure and the degrees thereof are in question. A player doesn't have to earn a soak roll, an Investigation roll to look over a crime scene, or whatever. The ST should be getting players to roll, because that means the ST is providing situations with dramatic tension where success, and failure have interesting stakes. If you're forcing your players to earn their rolls, your falling down on your job to actually provide scenarios that are dramatically interesting for the players to be in, in the first place.<br /> <br /> For social actions in particular, rolling after role-playing is detrimental to role-playing itself, because it creates a much greater dissonance than rolling first and RPing out the results. And is how the system generally works. Your character tries to do something. You roll. You role-play the results of whatever you tried. You don't role-play out all the twists and turns of a car chase and roll the dice after you've described the whole thing to see how it went. You get into a car chase, roll, and then role-play out the rolls' results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a player splats after a 200 meters you roll neither for damage nor soak, he's just dead. </div> </div> </div>Well, besides the laughable falling damage rules in the game, which would be unlikely to kill a mortal (seriously, look them up, humans should absolutely jump from 200m heights if they're in mortal danger if they don't jump, and Garou basically shouldn't care about falling at all), there's this thing call terminal velocity... once you hit it, the height you're falling stops mattering. Inflating the distance of the fall past that doesn't increase the fatality of the fall (and if you want to get technical falling from a farther height once terminal velocity is guaranteed can actually increase the odds of survival as you stop panicking and land as well as you're going to).<br /> <br /> If terminal velocity did 10 lethal levels of damage, a Garou should absolutely be allowed to call for a roll, because they can totally survive that. Just saying, &quot;nope you die, the fall is just too far&quot; is silly for anything that can soak lethal. Humans infrequently survive falls at terminal velocity, because despite the massive amount of force involved, there's a lot of factors that can mean the difference between splat, and survive but probably never walk again (though statistics on this are hard to come by, because a lot of people that fall from great heights are found dead without much of an ability to say if they died instantly on impact or survived and died from their injuries instead of directly from the impact).<br /> <br /> [quote]Also, only because they roll 15 dice versus 6 it doesn't mean that the statistics are in their favour, since you still need to take the action modifiers into account.[/quote[<br /> <br /> Well, &quot;dice&quot; instead of &quot;X + Y&quot; takes into account everything but difficulty modifiers, and yes, but considering that 15 dice with a specialty at diff 7 (so even if the base diff was 10, they can apply appropriate Gifts/Merits) will always have the statistical edge over 6 dice (though just barely against 6 dice with a specialty and diff 2). So there's that. But, you know, way to not at all engage with the point I was making!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You earn most of your renown questing around, away from your elders,... </div> </div> </div>Well, in specific styles of play this will certainly be the case, but there are others where it will not. The Sample Renown chart is full of things that can (and most times will) be in full view of the Sept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...so if things were as you're theorizing the Garou should: </div> </div> </div>You're going to need to explain this in more detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) earn Renown points only at the moots </div> </div> </div>Nope, nothing I said implies this at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) earn Renown points only based on what you tell at the moots. </div> </div> </div>Again, nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that's not how it happens. Somehow Gaia just knows, and maybe some peeking spirit too. Feel free to use social rolls as a renown shield for your characters if that suits your campaign, but it's really not how the Renown system was intended. </div> </div> </div>For someone bitching about me not reading the books, how about you read my posts before declaring them wrong?<br /> <br /> Also, if you actual care about making a point? Lets not get into the stupid, &quot;well at your table you can what you want, but by phrasing it like this you know what I mean to say is that you're a fucking moron so shut up and don't make points that might go against my view of things&quot; thing. It's very annoying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T10:03:14-07:00","id":1125944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125842#post1125842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except a large number of people have argued that PB's mechanics are fine, because the ST can just stop the abuse 'as needed' in play, not because of this whole &quot;earn your roll&quot; nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does this relate to me and what I was saying, like, at all? I think I wrote several times that PB rules are to be fixed, even proposed a few tweakings to make them more balanced.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if you actual care about making a point? </div> </div> </div>My point is that even with PB rules broken as they are you don't get to automatically win any situation, since any gimmick (as in Cat's exemple) should be naturally happen by the normal gameplay rules. Roll-playing is of course an exemple on how the gimmicks are not following a proper game item and of course saying that a storyteller will restrain the situation is not saving a bad rule, but roleplaying is also obviously supposed to happen in a controlled environment where rules do not override common sense.<br /> <br /> And yes, you largely implied that you can get out of Renown loss through social actions since you actually wrote: <i>&quot;There's also nebulous things like, do you lose Renown for breaking a rule, if your superiors don't consider you to have broken any rule&quot;</i>, so i spent a few words on that.<br /> <br /> And since you seem incapable of handling this discussion in a civilized manner any longer, I'm just done replying to you. My point is written all over these pages, I'll live by even if you don't get it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:42:06-07:00","id":1125994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125144#post1125144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That doesn't make it a false analogy though. Analogies, by their nature, involve comparing things that aren't the same, so there are bound to be differences. An analogy is false when the differences invalidate the core comparison.<br /> ...<br /> How does PB being a purely fictional trait invalidate the comparison the RPG abstractions of real traits? I might have never encountered PB IRL, but I've absolutely encountered people that believe in racial purity, and directly espoused a form of it where they're the superior ones, and I'm in the inferior category. So despite the fictional aspect of PB, it's not so outside human experience that the comparisons don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I know how analogies work, and I know what a false analogy is. When you advise me not to guess the motives of others in one post and then turn around and try to guess the quality of my education a couple of days later, it undermines your credibility. Now that I'm done being pseudo-offended, we may just have to disagree on how good your analogy is. :P<br /> <br /> Since you feel so strongly that Pure Breed encourages racism and/or classism in the game, do you have a similar feeling about how kinfolk and normal humans are treated as inferior species by the Litany? How about how there is less loss of renown associated with being disrespectful of the Bone Gnawers? To me these mechanical differences represent the &quot;orthodoxy&quot; of Garou society, but they don't necessarily indicate an ethical endorsement in the real world or in the World of Darkness setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> To everyone, Heavy Arms is right about the math: there is only <i>very</i> specific condition where adding a die to your roll actually reduces your odds of success, and that's when you go from rolling one die to rolling two dice against a difficulty of 2. In literally every other situation, adding dice helps your odds of success, and the only time adding dice will increase the odds of botching is when the difficulty is 10 -- but your odds of success are also going up at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:54:23-07:00","id":1126002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125842#post1125842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players aren't always up to acting their way through everything. &quot;My character should know the right thing to say, because they've got all the stats, but I'm having a brain fart,&quot; shouldn't be punished with, &quot;then you don't get to roll you horrible player!&quot; Because that's not fun, and this is a game. You don't hold back attack rolls because the player doesn't pick the right stance and attack direction to best strike around the opponents defenses. You just let them roll the attack. Same deal here.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> As well, players don't have to &quot;earn their roll.&quot; The rolls are there to abstract a situation where success, failure and the degrees thereof are in question. A player doesn't have to earn a soak roll, an Investigation roll to look over a crime scene, or whatever. The ST should be getting players to roll, because that means the ST is providing situations with dramatic tension where success, and failure have interesting stakes. If you're forcing your players to earn their rolls, your falling down on your job to actually provide scenarios that are dramatically interesting for the players to be in, in the first place.<br /> <br /> For social actions in particular, rolling after role-playing is detrimental to role-playing itself, because it creates a much greater dissonance than rolling first and RPing out the results. And is how the system generally works. Your character tries to do something. You roll. You role-play the results of whatever you tried. You don't role-play out all the twists and turns of a car chase and roll the dice after you've described the whole thing to see how it went. You get into a car chase, roll, and then role-play out the rolls' results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to &quot;like&quot; the whole post, but this part I definitely agree with. Nobody should be penalized because they don't have 5 dots worth of charisma or empathy in real life any more than they should be penalized because they don't have 5 dots worth of appearance or intelligence in real life. &quot;Get up and dance for your success on that performance roll&quot; isn't something any sane storyteller would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:12:27-07:00","id":1126034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem#post1123755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd prefer for it to be removed from the game. Thoughts on this? It's not the first time I've heard people claim PB is broken, or doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purebreed is a badly written mechanic. Its one of those &quot;what they were thinking?&quot; moments on WW design that might made sense back then in the 90s.....maybe.... probably not but that is just so bad that not even insight covers its. Its up there with multiaction with rage, those &quot;fuck you i win&quot; gifts, enchanting voice, the shitty multiactions rules that keep appearing on the 20th lines instead of the good ones and shapeshifting rolls.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> has proven how bad it is on the mechanical side already. What i have done in my game is just make it so how is more or less suppose to work.<br /> <br /> In my game PB is only how likely are you to breed a Garou, that it. More pure breed more chances of fathering/mothering a true born. Nothing else.<br /> <br /> This means that in some tribes is way more useful than another. I read the argument that PB explains how the SF keep their power and i said that they do that because of both infrastructure and organization than said, the BGs.<br /> <br /> The BGs are more populous and have a higher total number of true borns than the SF. However the infrastructure of the SF meant that when a SF is true born he already starts educated and with the resources at his disposal than the BGs who most likely start as lost cubs.<br /> <br /> Setting wise is the same, can the typical PCs that dont play by the rules ignore the Silver Fangs? Sure you can but also keep in mind that they have friends and a social context that make it so that ignoring them is costly even when they are plain wrong. What it isnt needed is poorly designed mechanics to enforce it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-07-2017, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:21:55-07:00","id":1126039,"title":"","content":"From a mechanical stand-point, I see it as something for the PCs who want be social monkeys to twink themselves.<br /> <br /> Like Firearms 5.<br /> <br /> But for Garou interactions.<br /> <br /> It's part of the power fantasy.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are the most important looking guy in the room.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:37:42-07:00","id":1126048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126039#post1126039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a mechanical stand-point, I see it as something for the PCs who want be social monkeys to twink themselves.<br /> <br /> Like Firearms 5.<br /> <br /> But for Garou interactions.<br /> <br /> It's part of the power fantasy.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are the most important looking guy in the room.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is but at it also adds to challenges is like a combat/social/advancement stat all rolled into 1 with the low cost of background points. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:39:07-07:00","id":1126050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126048#post1126048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is but at it also adds to challenges is like a combat/social/advancement stat all rolled into 1 with the low cost of background points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is a bit too much done there.<br /> <br /> How to tweak it is the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:41:38-07:00","id":1126053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126050#post1126050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, there is a bit too much done there.<br /> <br /> How to tweak it is the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already wrote how i did it. If a PC wants to be a social min-maxer there are other OP merits he can take that are not as broken (though still pretty broken) as PB, like Enchanting voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-07-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:47:12-07:00","id":1126057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origina