eonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T14:54:41-07:00","id":1126062,"title":"","content":"Just restrict the bonus to when you are dealing with other members of your Tribe. The Silver Fangs then rule because Silver Fangs stand together against other Tribes rather than because of social bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T15:02:51-07:00","id":1126064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126057#post1126057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I'm asking how to keep Pure Breed as a major part of Garou culture with all its Unfortunate Implications intact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like i wrote, Purebreed is also strictly tied to how likely is the Garou to produce a true born child which in a culture dedicated to fighting and reproducing is very important.<br /> <br /> The implication of Purebreed in that case is still relevant because the higher PB Garou and kin in a tribe has more members it has. Thats why SF are the kings of the game (normally) because they both have such a standardized process for pure breed and organization behind it that when a Garou changes into the tribe it starts with all the advantages.<br /> <br /> The duels and nepotism is still very present and dont need a mechanical counterpart in the form of +dices to social interaction for Purebreed to be relevant.<br /> <br /> Why doesnt the Party ignore the snobby silver fang that doesnt take as much risk as them? Because said snobby silver fang is more valuable in the long term than the rest of the party be that because when he/she mates is more likely to produce a garou. Also because the Silver Fangs got the best fetish, the best organization, etc.<br /> <br /> Or you can go the route of Forsaken and use their version of Purebreed<br /> <br /> &quot;Effect: Your character is the perfect likeness of one of ideal of the tribe. She looks the part so very closely that she shakes the souls of her onlookers. Choose an Attribute that reflects her relationship to the Firstborn. She gains a dot in that Attribute, and that Attribute can go one above the normal maximum normally six dots.<br /> <br /> Drawback: Your character draws unwanted attention. Wrathful spirits with old memories will attempt to settle old scores with her likeness, through her.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is also an ability on the merit that allows to leave impose your purebreed to avoid onlookers to attack the character via spending 1 WP and imposing the shaken condition. However the shaken condition doesnt do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-07-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T03:22:43-07:00","id":1126240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125944#post1125944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how does this relate to me and what I was saying, like, at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>See all the text below what you quoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point is that even with PB rules broken as they are you don't get to automatically win any situation, since any gimmick (as in Cat's exemple) should be naturally happen by the normal gameplay rules. </div> </div> </div>The difference between &quot;automatically win,&quot; and, &quot;win 95% of the time,&quot; seems a meaningless distinction to the point of all this. As well, the example in question isn't a demonstration of a &quot;gimmick.&quot; It's a character doing something stupid, but doing it very well. It does nothing to address a character that's actually throwing their social steamroller capabilities around in a fashion that actually benefits them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Roll-playing is of course an exemple on how the gimmicks are not following a proper game item and of course saying that a storyteller will restrain the situation is not saving a bad rule, but roleplaying is also obviously supposed to happen in a controlled environment where rules do not override common sense. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Roll-playing&quot; is a strawman constructed for Internet debates to either side-step points about mechanical flaws in the game (&quot;That doesn't matter, because you're roll-playing instead of role-playing, and a role-player wouldn't be concerned about mechanics like that&quot;), or worse to just put down play-styles in an ad hominem fashion (&quot;Pfft. Who cares, that guy's just a dumb roll-player that doesn't give a shit about role-playing like us real RPG fans, ignore him.&quot;).<br /> <br /> And &quot;the controlled environment&quot; of an RPG <b>is the rules</b>. Rules that regularly override common sense, to the point where the ST needs to step in and override the rules? Those are bad rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, you largely implied that you can get out of Renown loss through social actions since you actually wrote: <i>&quot;There's also nebulous things like, do you lose Renown for breaking a rule, if your superiors don't consider you to have broken any rule&quot;</i>, so i spent a few words on that. </div> </div> </div>I qualified, and I've expanded on and explained that qualified point. Repeatedly acting as if I implied an absolute simply isn't posting in good faith.<br /> <br /> Neither is, again, cutting off my posts and acting like there isn't a sentence or more right after what you quoted that is pretty important to the context there.<br /> <br /> Yes, I said that, but snipping it out of context to make me look bad is silly on a forum thread. My point there remains extremely valid. The Renown awards include multiple examples that are based on other character's perceptions of your character. So the spirits <b>care about what other people think</b>, and do not just coldly apply the &quot;letter&quot; of the law on you. There is absolutely a nebulous point in the rules here. Questioning a leader in a time of war is breaking the Litany... but that requires the leader to honestly consider it a time of war and feel the question was out of line. Also the whole Punishment rite thing requires a Garou to enact the rite, which means a Garou that can be convinced not to The spirits can't hit you with Punishment rite penalties of their own will.<br /> <br /> And you didn't say a single word on any of that. You just start in on how that supposedly implies everything happens at a Moot. Which doesn't make a lick of sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And since you seem incapable of handling this discussion in a civilized manner any longer,... </div> </div> </div>I'll continue to respond within limits to the level of civility I feel like I'm getting in return. Don't confuse a lack of profanity with being civil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125994#post1125994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you advise me not to guess the motives of others in one post and then turn around and try to guess the quality of my education a couple of days later, it undermines your credibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am 100% honestly not sure if you seriously mean this, or if this is a joke being killed by a purely text based medium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...we may just have to disagree on how good your analogy is. </div> </div> </div>You could... actually expand on your reasoning? You said it was a false analogy for reason X. I countered with why I don't think reason X qualifies as a false analogy. You haven't rebutted or rephrased your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since you feel so strongly that Pure Breed encourages racism and/or classism in the game, do you have a similar feeling about how kinfolk and normal humans are treated as inferior species by the Litany? How about how there is less loss of renown associated with being disrespectful of the Bone Gnawers? To me these mechanical differences represent the &quot;orthodoxy&quot; of Garou society, but they don't necessarily indicate an ethical endorsement in the real world or in the World of Darkness setting. </div> </div> </div>First off, I have been avoiding drawing a parallel between PB and racism. The closest I came was saying enthno-nationalism. I've been drawing that line in my posts for a reason.<br /> <br /> Second, I feel strongly that PB deals with classism <b>poorly</b> by making it metaphysically true in the system. High class Garou are inherently superior to low class Garou, instead classism existing in the game as a social construct that could potentially be fought (though the systemic nature of Garou hierarchical society makes that a very tough hill to climb). Things like the Litany are much better for broaching these topics. The Litany, for example, never actually says Kinfolk and humans are inferior species. That's a common way Garou interpret the Litany to justify their actions, but it's actually contrary to the Litany as a whole. The Litany focuses on &quot;station&quot; rather than an inherent level of superiority/inferiority, as station can be won or lost. Especially regarding Kinfolk, Garou society, not the Litany, denies them station that could allow them equal or superior status to Garou. The Litany also only applies to members of the Garou Nation. Ronin and BSDs can largely ignore the Litany baring the Nation being upset about it and acting on that upset (which... they were going to do anyway). If two gay Garou go Ronin so they can openly be together and ignore the first tenant of the Litany, they suffer no consequences beyond going Ronin. They can stay home and violate the Litany every night without the spirits doing anything extra to them. Pure Breed, on the other hand, keeps working on all Garou. PB allows a Garou to be better at trying to intimidate BSDs in the midst of battle, or convince a traveling Ronin to do something for the Sept on the down-low, because even the Wyrm's servants and the outcasts can't ignore the mystical power of PB.<br /> <br /> That's what bugs me the most about PB on a thematic level. It doesn't just introduce classism/etc. into the game. It enshrines it as a truth of the setting that - at least in Garou society - classism is justified; rather than classism just being a thing that Garou internally justify in their cultural norms, and systemically enforced by those that benefit from it. Not that PB introduces the themes in general.<br /> <br /> I want these things to just be the orthodoxy of Garou society, but that's not how PB works.<br /> <br /> And I don't think (nor have I said anything to this) that the books are trying to endorse classism. I think like many issues with WtA in particular, the political messages in the game are so hamfisted (esp. in early editions) that they backfire. The whole, &quot;things would be better if all the Tribes could get along&quot; appeal to diversity is hampered by how problematic most of the Tribes are for representing the human ethnic/social groups they're linked to. Likewise, PB backfires trying to make the Garou so blinded by their cultural obsession with lineage that they ignore their classism, by making lineage so awesome they're right to be obsessed with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126039#post1126039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a mechanical stand-point, I see it as something for the PCs who want be social monkeys to twink themselves.<br /> <br /> Like Firearms 5.<br /> <br /> But for Garou interactions.<br /> <br /> It's part of the power fantasy.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are the most important looking guy in the room.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't quite work though, because the equivalent of Firearms 5 is something like Leadership 5; not Purebreed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T04:24:04-07:00","id":1126255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126240#post1126240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't quite work though because the equivalent of Firearms 5 is something like Leadership 5; not Purebreed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Status 5 among vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T06:55:11-07:00","id":1126285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126240#post1126240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I feel strongly that PB deals with classism <b>poorly</b> by making it metaphysically true in the system. High class Garou are inherently superior to low class Garou, instead classism existing in the game as a social construct that could potentially be fought (though the systemic nature of Garou hierarchical society makes that a very tough hill to climb). Things like the Litany are much better for broaching these topics. The Litany, for example, never actually says Kinfolk and humans are inferior species. That's a common way Garou interpret the Litany to justify their actions, but it's actually contrary to the Litany as a whole. The Litany focuses on &quot;station&quot; rather than an inherent level of superiority/inferiority, as station can be won or lost. Especially regarding Kinfolk, Garou society, not the Litany, denies them station that could allow them equal or superior status to Garou. The Litany also only applies to members of the Garou Nation. Ronin and BSDs can largely ignore the Litany baring the Nation being upset about it and acting on that upset (which... they were going to do anyway). If two gay Garou go Ronin so they can openly be together and ignore the first tenant of the Litany, they suffer no consequences beyond going Ronin. They can stay home and violate the Litany every night without the spirits doing anything extra to them. Pure Breed, on the other hand, keeps working on all Garou. PB allows a Garou to be better at trying to intimidate BSDs in the midst of battle, or convince a traveling Ronin to do something for the Sept on the down-low, because even the Wyrm's servants and the outcasts can't ignore the mystical power of PB.<br /> <br /> That's what bugs me the most about PB on a thematic level. It doesn't just introduce classism/etc. into the game. It enshrines it as a truth of the setting that - at least in Garou society - classism is justified; rather than classism just being a thing that Garou internally justify in their cultural norms, and systemically enforced by those that benefit from it. Not that PB introduces the themes in general.<br /> <br /> I want these things to just be the orthodoxy of Garou society, but that's not how PB works.<br /> <br /> And I don't think (nor have I said anything to this) that the books are trying to endorse classism. I think like many issues with WtA in particular, the political messages in the game are so hamfisted (esp. in early editions) that they backfire. The whole, &quot;things would be better if all the Tribes could get along&quot; appeal to diversity is hampered by how problematic most of the Tribes are for representing the human ethnic/social groups they're linked to. Likewise, PB backfires trying to make the Garou so blinded by their cultural obsession with lineage that they ignore their classism, by making lineage so awesome they're right to be obsessed with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree on part of this, i like that PB is a objectively truth on the setting. Not the mechanics of it, like i mentioned in my post even if just related to how likely a true born is to be born.<br /> <br /> Because it gives the Garou nation a point that otherwise would sorely lack. Make their abominable action have at least one slight point that cannot be constested and that gives them more nuanced.<br /> <br /> Whenever i refer to the asshole tribes (Fianna, Silver Fangs, etc etc) i purposedly choose the word asshole instead of evil because to gamers in general there is a distinct difference between evil and asshole with the latter being worse.<br /> <br /> I put you an evil character say Thanos vs The red Skull and people will dislike the red skull way more because he is a nazi and being racist or part of any type of hate group is considered far worse than been a killer (Regardless of scale). Maybe it makes sense maybe it doesnt but is something pretty ingrained in western society.<br /> <br /> So when presenting the Garou nation with all its flaws is easy for the PC groups who normally plays progressive garous born outside of the nation to just dismiss their PB notion and classicism by saying &quot;Thats wrong, get on with the times.&quot; and paint their line on the sand and be the &quot;Big Damn Heroes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Its another matter when the argument is <br /> -&quot;Thats wrong, get on with the times.&quot;<br /> -&quot;No it isnt, is objectively true for our/your species&quot;<br /> <br /> Now this introduces a moral question that we dont face. PB being an objective truth makes harder to dismiss it. It doesnt validates it completely either because one only has to look at the Garou history as also objective proof that the classicism of nation is a hidrance. <br /> <br /> So to me, it makes the moral issues of Werewolf more complex. It gives a supposition remove enough from reality that makes the moral question one that isnt as black and white as in reality.<br /> <br /> It moves the goal post beyond &quot;Classicism/Racism is this social obsolete construct of the nation&quot; to &quot;classicism/Racism of the nation used to serve a function, is time to reconsider if it has outlive is usefulness and now is a hidrance&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:22:56-07:00","id":1126294,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of TITLE in Changeling: The Dreaming which I think affects my opinion of Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> In Changeling, Title has numerous mechanical and social benefits.<br /> <br /> Even as it's in a society where Feudalism is B.S. social construct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:20:08-07:00","id":1126350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126240#post1126240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am 100% honestly not sure if you seriously mean this, or if this is a joke being killed by a purely text based medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of both. I'm trying not to take myself too seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126240#post1126240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could... actually expand on your reasoning? You said it was a false analogy for reason X. I countered with why I don't think reason X qualifies as a false analogy. You haven't rebutted or rephrased your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. For context, here's your original counter-argument.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1125144#post1125144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does PB being a purely fictional trait invalidate the comparison the RPG abstractions of real traits? I might have never encountered PB IRL, but I've absolutely encountered people that believe in racial purity, and directly espoused a form of it where they're the superior ones, and I'm in the inferior category. So despite the fictional aspect of PB, it's not so outside human experience that the comparisons don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually where I got the idea you were comparing Pure Breed and racism. I don't consider the Pure Breed background as classism either, which why I don't think the analogy works. To me, Pure Breed is something that characters respond to instinctively and intuitively, rather than rationally. Imagine if you were at a bar and George Costanza (the character from Seinfeld) walked in. Now imagine if Quinn the Eskimo from the Bob Dylan song walked in, or if you don't know that song, imagine Joe Namath. Now imagine if Conor McGregor walked in. You'd have a much easier time ignoring, disrespecting, or rejecting Costanza than Quinn, Namath, or McGregor, whether or not you knew who any of them were. The vibe would instinctive and visceral, in each case, but it would have nothing to do with race or social class. I think this kind of personal magnetism, more related to physical beauty, athleticism, charisma, confidence, etc., is a better real-world analogy to Pure Breed than classism. On the other hand, Pure Breed is also a spiritual vibe that invokes a gnostic memory of ancestors, for which I don't think the human world has any good analogy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126240#post1126240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> That's what bugs me the most about PB on a thematic level. It doesn't just introduce classism/etc. into the game. It enshrines it as a truth of the setting that - at least in Garou society - classism is justified; rather than classism just being a thing that Garou internally justify in their cultural norms, and systemically enforced by those that benefit from it. Not that PB introduces the themes in general.<br /> <br /> I want these things to just be the orthodoxy of Garou society, but that's not how PB works.<br /> <br /> And I don't think (nor have I said anything to this) that the books are trying to endorse classism. I think like many issues with WtA in particular, the political messages in the game are so hamfisted (esp. in early editions) that they backfire. The whole, &quot;things would be better if all the Tribes could get along&quot; appeal to diversity is hampered by how problematic most of the Tribes are for representing the human ethnic/social groups they're linked to. Likewise, PB backfires trying to make the Garou so blinded by their cultural obsession with lineage that they ignore their classism, by making lineage so awesome they're right to be obsessed with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, Pure Breed isn't something that is &quot;justified&quot; or that Garou are &quot;obsessed with.&quot; It describes a natural trait of the species without appeal to or need for any justification. It's more like the advantages of being one of the Beautiful People* in human society, that may not be fair or justifiable, but for better or worse, it's real.<br /> <br /> *See <i><a href=\"http://www.businessinsider.com/studies-show-the-advantages-of-being-beautiful-2013-6\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.businessinsider.com/studi...autiful-2013-6</a></i> and <i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93DYxrQg3b8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93DYxrQg3b8</a> </i>for reference to the advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:58:47-07:00","id":1126372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126350#post1126350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, Pure Breed isn't something that is &quot;justified&quot; or that Garou are &quot;obsessed with.&quot; It describes a natural trait of the species without appeal to or need for any justification. It's more like the advantages of being one of the Beautiful People* in human society, that may not be fair or justifiable, but for better or worse, it's real.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just plain false. You wanna downplay it in your setting thats fine but the Garou Nation is obsessed with Purebreed. Kinfolk are allowed or disallowed to mate because of Purebreed, a wrong type of purebreed is a stigma to live by.<br /> <br /> Even the two tribes who reject purebreed in a sense (GWs and BGs) are partly defined by their rejection of it. And even if you put it on the &quot;like appearance&quot; analogy it falls appart because there is never context on Purebreed. The way it mechanically works is the same no matter the garou/kinfolk onlooker.<br /> <br /> While appearance/charisma/confidence depends on our bias. So in you example of George Constanza vs all of the above for example it would work differently for me than you because i have a negative bias versus beautiful/charismatic/confident people and i would dismiss them instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-08-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T16:16:33-07:00","id":1126496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126372#post1126372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the two tribes who reject purebreed in a sense (GWs and BGs) are partly defined by their rejection of it. And even if you put it on the &quot;like appearance&quot; analogy it falls appart because there is never context on Purebreed. The way it mechanically works is the same no matter the garou/kinfolk onlooker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, I agree that my analogy isn't very good either. It's difficult for our human minds to imagine how the aura of a werewolf's heroic ancestors could be viscerally apparent to other werewolves in his presence, but to me that makes it easier to accept its having a mechanical effect on social interactions. To borrow a line from William Blake, &quot;one law for the lion and ox is oppression.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126372#post1126372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While appearance/charisma/confidence depends on our bias. So in you example of George Constanza vs all of the above for example it would work differently for me than you because i have a negative bias versus beautiful/charismatic/confident people and i would dismiss them instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be just like, my opinion, man, but the research I cited in my footnote suggests that someone with a bias <i>against</i> &quot;beautiful people&quot; is uncommon enough to be noteworthy in a random crowd of humans. The same might be said of a werewolf who is biased against &quot;pure bred&quot; Garou, and could justify something about his or her personality that you could find a place for on the character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:06:37-07:00","id":1126526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126496#post1126496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same might be said of a werewolf who is biased against &quot;pure bred&quot; Garou, and could justify something about his or her personality that you could find a place for on the character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except thats impossible per raw, context, personality and past experience are irrelevant for the effect that Purebreed has on a Garou (Houserules not withstanding). To the point that even the Black Spiral dancers, Garou that walk a mystical spiral of madness are not inmune to it.<br /> <br /> I could make the most Purebreed hating BGs garou in the world and he will still be affected by Purebreed just like any other Garou in the same exact way. Thats why it isnt &quot;just like any other social attribute&quot; because it literary forces a white room situation in which context is irrelevant beyond &quot;is this persona a human or a kinfolk/Garou&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T20:31:45-07:00","id":1126571,"title":"","content":"Purely by HOUSE RULES, here is how I run Pure Breed, i.e. &quot;The Racist Pure Breed.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Pure Breed is a purely social construct of the Garou Nation that has no effect outside of interactions with members, with Black Spiral Dancers, Ronin, and certain urbanized Garou (at the ST's discretion) being immune. It reflects the cultural baggage the Garou have with history and lineage as well as some genuinely ethnocentric ideas of how a Garou &quot;should&quot; look in both their Homid as well as Lupus and Crinos forms. It has only the barest of mystical components and does not confer any respect with spirits or Fera. Garou who possess Pure Breed scores can add each dice to Leadership, Persuasion, Intimidation, and Subterfuge rolls (with the assumption Pure Bred werewolves are inherently more trustworthy). Unlike renown, a Garou with Pure Breed never has to worry about losing said status but will be judged to a somewhat harsher standard with offenses leading to stiffer penalties with less &quot;promising&quot; candidates.</i></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:39:31-07:00","id":1126586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126255#post1126255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking Status 5 among vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>If PB worked like Status (closer to many of our posted house rules) this comparison would work better. The design intent might have been to share a similar space as status, but I've never heard any developer confirm that. They're both social oriented backgrounds, but they work pretty differently RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126285#post1126285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree on part of this, i like that PB is a objectively truth on the setting. Not the mechanics of it, like i mentioned in my post even if just related to how likely a true born is to be born.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind PB if house ruled, because those house rules tend to remove the issues I have with how the RAW interact with the themes the background deals in.<br /> <br /> Like my own house rule posted up thread where I split it into two Backgrounds. My Heritage concept is, like PB, something you just have, but it lacks the &quot;high PB characters are inherently superior&quot; thing because the bonuses aren't universal to all Garou, and the increased likelihood of breeding is (since I tend to ignore the books that put numbers to this) both nebulous and only &quot;superior&quot; in a social context. A Silver Fang might be more likely to have trueborn kids from a monogamous arranged marriage, but a Bonegnawer can compensate by having a ton of kids from a bunch of partners to effectively create the same number of trueborn children. Both strategies have pros and cons to them, even if Garou society is heavily biased towards mated pairs.<br /> <br /> The objectivity that gets me is the social bonus of all-Garou application.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it gives the Garou nation a point that otherwise would sorely lack. Make their abominable action have at least one slight point that cannot be constested and that gives them more nuanced. </div> </div> </div>I'm also not sure I agree with the idea that the Garou are lacking in objective truths to hang their cultural justifications on. They have direct interaction with the spirits, including their Tribal Totems (if rarely) and possibly even their primary deities in Gaia and Luna (exceedingly rarely). Having the spirits watching, judging, and rewarding/punishing/aiding them is already a fairly huge objective thing to hang stuff on. You can't deny the objective truth that the Garou are rewarded for many of their actions we find morally reprehensible by the spirits they consider the source of their cultural morality. They don't have to take such things on faith, (or humanism style ethical assumptions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now this introduces a moral question that we dont face. PB being an objective truth makes harder to dismiss it. It doesnt validates it completely either because one only has to look at the Garou history as also objective proof that the classicism of nation is a hidrance. </div> </div> </div>That's... not really a question though. That's more of a cultural dilemma.<br /> <br /> As well, why do we need PB for this? Falcon can just show up and say, &quot;The Silver Fangs are born of noble blood, and chosen by the spirits to rule the Garou Nation.&quot; to add everything PB does without it as a trait to this issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126350#post1126350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, Pure Breed is something that characters respond to instinctively and intuitively, rather than rationally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classism isn't perpetuated by rationality, because IRL it isn't rational. Just like physical appearance, social norms associated with signs of class vastly impact subconscious impressions.<br /> <br /> There was an amusing Mythbusters episode (which is backed up by more formal studies, but it's way more fun to watch) where they have large groups of women rate the attractiveness of men based on pictures with some demographic information (job, kind of home, location of home). The pictures remained the same, but the demographics were changed between sampling. Higher paying jobs, and better living conditions, always increased attraction ratings despite the same visuals.<br /> <br /> Interviews with their test groups even revealed that the women were generally aware of such biases, but acted on them anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this kind of personal magnetism, more related to physical beauty, athleticism, charisma, confidence, etc., is a better real-world analogy to Pure Breed than classism. On the other hand, Pure Breed is also a spiritual vibe that invokes a gnostic memory of ancestors, for which I don't think the human world has any good analogy. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the game has a (poorly implemented) trait for this: Appearance. Appearance is a general trait anyone can take.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed's problem is that it isn't just super-Appearance, because it's linked to &quot;class&quot; in the form of Tribes and family ties that make up the classes in Garou Society. The Gnawers and Glasswalkers are Urrah Tribes, and those the lowest class of Garou society, and denied PB completely. Silver Fangs are explicitly the royal Tribe that maintain noble bloodlines to maximize PB, and as the highest class of Garou society, they have to take it.<br /> <br /> That's how the classism part comes in. PB's distribution is directly linked to class in Garou society. Even in all the Tribes in-between, higher PB characters are given more social standing, and the &quot;middle class&quot; Tribes still have to play the PB game to maintain that social standing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way I see it, Pure Breed isn't something that is &quot;justified&quot; or that Garou are &quot;obsessed with.&quot; It describes a natural trait of the species without appeal to or need for any justification. It's more like the advantages of being one of the Beautiful People* in human society, that may not be fair or justifiable, but for better or worse, it's real. </div> </div> </div>It does, however, completely lack the nuances that things like visual appearance have in terms of impact. Especially since beauty is a social construct, what one group considers a sign of attractiveness is not what all humans will respond to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:53:27-07:00","id":1126593,"title":"","content":"I actually agree with you on that Heavy Arms, which is why I use it.<br /> <br /> You need stuff for players to get pissed off about in Garou Society.<br /> <br /> And yes, I dislike the whole, &quot;And it is spiritually true and not related to appearance or Homid appearance at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, I hated the idea Garou didn't reincarnate too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T04:02:39-07:00","id":1126647,"title":"","content":"For me, my purebreed headcanon relates to what the tribes have to do to -have- those looks.<br /> <br /> For example;<br /> <br /> Silent Striders have very short fur, they may have an undercoat, but they generally do not take to colder weather well. Then again, due to breeding for solid black coats, days in the desert are not exactly fun, either.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs breed for a white coat and blue eyes, essentially risking massive deafness and blindness among themselves. What is more, due to the various houses living in different areas, they have to nearly line breed to keep their coats white and eyes blue.<br /> <br /> Wendigo meanwhile relies on spiritual ties with their totem, and to a mutation to keep their purebreed looks. Essentially, to get a white haired and blue/purple eyed person from Inuit and Yupik stock, they need to be leucistic to match the looks. Due to Wendigo's influence, their fur is not reddish but bluish. But things like light sensitivity and sunburns are still common.<br /> <br /> For Black Furies, Shadow Lords and Red Talons, their looks come from favouring certain mutations of colour. For the Talons, this means mainly reddish coats. For Furies, clear markings of black and white are favoured. And the Lords? Well, if they look a bit dog-like with their pure black coats, that is acceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:57:30-07:00","id":1126684,"title":"","content":"While I might be sounding like a broken drum, I think that the solution for the Garou is just to have Pure Breed influence social interactions with Garou and Kinfolk of your Tribe. Since the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers are more meritocratic than other Garou Tribes, they do not have Pure Breed. In addition, change Pure Breed for Kinfolk from reproductive bonus to a similar social bonus, and just change the reproductive probability. <br /> <br /> In that framework, Garou would have a 10% chance of producing Garou with normal humans (40% chance of producing Kinfolk) and a 20% chance of producing Garou with Kinfolk (80% chance of producing Kinfolk). Kinfolk would have a 2% chance of producing Garou with normal humans (40% chance of producing Kinfolk) and a 4% chance of producing Garou with Kinfolk (80% chance of producing Kinfolk). I think that these two changes would balance Pure Breed and give a real reason for Garou of every Tribe to prefer mating with Kinfolk (and for preferring Kinfolk to breed with Kinfolk) without the weirdness of Pure Breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:12:12-07:00","id":1127015,"title":"","content":"When people talk about about the classism involved in Pure Breed, I think they're looking at the wrong type of classism. It's not the 'steampunk' classism with snobby delusional nobles. Noo, it's the tribal version of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Film/Gattaca\" target=\"_blank\">Gattaca</a> classism, where people are thrown into the underclass because have fewer of such-and-such inborn advantages (lost the genetic/spiritual lottery). And we do have to consider: if there are inheritable inborn semi-spiritual traits that make one more talented at socially influencing other werewolves and their kin, then wouldn't it be a logical consequence that the weres and kin would obsess about such a trait? And would it not be logical for those possessing such talents to try to convince everyone that such talents are a marker of greatness (and rather successfully, thanks to all the bonus dice)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","user":"vicky_molokh","date":". 08-10-2017, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T17:36:24-07:00","id":1127410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1126064#post1126064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like i wrote, Purebreed is also strictly tied to how likely is the Garou to produce a true born child which in a culture dedicated to fighting and reproducing is very important.<br /> <br /> The implication of Purebreed in that case is still relevant because the higher PB Garou and kin in a tribe has more members it has. Thats why SF are the kings of the game (normally) because they both have such a standardized process for pure breed and organization behind it that when a Garou changes into the tribe it starts with all the advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like it, since it seems to have virtually no impact on the common gameplay (unless you make a campaing focused on breeding... not so thrilling to me) and only a scent of importance at a background level. Yes, Silver Fangs may now have more garou than the rest of the tribes now and therefore be the strongest one, but I don't really see all that important to the character, it looks more like an NPC trait.<br /> It would change a fair bit of the game background too, as I previously wrote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Effect: Your character is the perfect likeness of one of ideal of the tribe. She looks the part so very closely that she shakes the souls of her onlookers. Choose an Attribute that reflects her relationship to the Firstborn. She gains a dot in that Attribute, and that Attribute can go one above the normal maximum normally six dots. </div> </div> </div>This is a bit better, but it should be a merit and not a background. I kinda like the social aspect in the PB though, I would not remove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that the solution for the Garou is just to have Pure Breed influence social interactions with Garou and Kinfolk of your Tribe </div> </div> </div>There would be no point in the Silver Fangs tribe requirement though, and way less reasons to stay strong on their breeding program.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127015#post1127015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people talk about about the classism involved in Pure Breed, I think they're looking at the wrong type of classism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly think they are not experienced enough to detach their character from theirselves. It's not an issue or a point of shame <i>per se</i>, we all started somewhere and we all have subjects we are not comfortable with. But while SJW are deeply needed in countries like Turkey, China and Sudan I'd argue that an RPG forum is definitely not their place. I strongly encourage them to fight for human rights in places where people can actually benefit from it rather than where it's only useful to boost their ego.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And we do have to consider: if there are inheritable inborn semi-spiritual traits that make one more talented at socially influencing other werewolves and their kin, then wouldn't it be a logical consequence that the weres and kin would obsess about such a trait? And would it not be logical for those possessing such talents to try to convince everyone that such talents are a marker of greatness (and rather successfully, thanks to all the bonus dice)? </div> </div> </div>I like this utilitarian PB view too. Whether for real or make-believe, the Garou think that a pure descendent from great heroes has more chances to be great too (better ancestors to call upon, better fetishes as heritage, better lessons passed on father to son, etc), and maybe they even think they inherit part of their ancestors' strengths and heroism. Yes, they're nobility and that means they have more resources, you'd better take them into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T17:39:09-07:00","id":1127411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aCv10_WvGxo\" data-code=\"aCv10_WvGxo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aCv10_WvGxo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T18:06:38-07:00","id":1127417,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone cares that much about Pure Breed except how it influences their enjoyment of the game. It's about as important as whether or not it's okay to be racist against orcs. Ergo, it's a valid thing to discuss on forums as a storytelling tool but nothing to get worked up over.<br /> <br /> And yes, Pure Breed actually being a sign your character is inbred as fuck is basically the Silver Fangs isn't it?<br /> <br /> I mean, the whole &quot;Silver Fangs are crazy because of a CURSE&quot; is a silly retcon versus them being severely delusional Hapsburgs with too much of an entitlement complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T19:45:47-07:00","id":1127454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127417#post1127417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone cares that much about Pure Breed (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you write more about the reasons that make you think it is so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T20:39:17-07:00","id":1127466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127410#post1127410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like it, since it seems to have virtually no impact on the common gameplay</div> </div> </div> </div>I see nothing wrong with that. Its cutting the problematic mechanic all together. And it can affect common gameplay outside of the act of breeding. For example in certain negotiations or dealings with tribes that care specially about strong family lines but what it wouldnt be is an abolute &quot;this works always like this regardless of context&quot; kind of mechanic<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127410#post1127410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit better, but it should be a merit and not a background. I kinda like the social aspect in the PB though, I would not remove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction between Background and Merit is largely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127410#post1127410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly think they are not experienced enough to detach their character from theirselves. It's not an issue or a point of shame <i>per se</i>, we all started somewhere and we all have subjects we are not comfortable with. But while SJW are deeply needed in countries like Turkey, China and Sudan I'd argue that an RPG forum is definitely not their place. I strongly encourage them to fight for human rights in places where people can actually benefit from it rather than where it's only useful to boost their ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? What SJW have anything to do with this? PB is a type of classicism there is no question about it. It doesnt make the game &quot;bad&quot; because of it because its part of the game the fight against said classicism. Its part of the conflict and is there. But the big majority of people that have issue with it dont do that because of the classicism but because the mechanics of it are trainwreck of poor design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T22:12:13-07:00","id":1127485,"title":"","content":"I wonder why the trait was created in the first place? I suspect it might have been a way to compensate for werewolves being mostly physical. Take this background and you have powerful socials despite being social tertiary. It also might have been intended to create a stronger distinction between your human life and your garou life. In your human life, you're this social tertiary character with ugly battlescars and a general creepy feral vibe. But once you go amongst the other garou, you are a hero of the ages, adored as you sally forth to slay banes in the umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T02:08:56-07:00","id":1127525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127454#post1127454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you write more about the reasons that make you think it is so?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense of being I've seen huge thousands of internet posts where people completely lose their shit over changes to campaign settings or new editions. This is mostly, &quot;it's not working for me&quot; and &quot;It should be different.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not an element of the setting which I think anyone thinks is ABSOLUTELY NECESSARY.<br /> <br /> But it's one some like and others don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T02:27:37-07:00","id":1127528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127525#post1127525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) It's not an element of the setting which I think anyone thinks is ABSOLUTELY NECESSARY. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T03:15:54-07:00","id":1127539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127417#post1127417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, Pure Breed actually being a sign your character is inbred as fuck is basically the Silver Fangs isn't it?<br /> <br /> I mean, the whole &quot;Silver Fangs are crazy because of a CURSE&quot; is a silly retcon versus them being severely delusional Hapsburgs with too much of an entitlement complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the world of WtA, genetics and spiritual curses are not necessarily easily separable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T03:20:30-07:00","id":1127541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127539#post1127539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the world of WtA, genetics and spiritual curses are not necessarily easily separable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you say in which W:tA books this is written? Could you give page numbers, or chapters' names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T04:03:36-07:00","id":1127554,"title":"","content":"As someone who draws a lot of WtA art, purebreed is something I like to use in the setting. Plus, as someone who has interest in canine genetics, the way PB manifests and wha it means can be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T04:24:43-07:00","id":1127560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-d