 <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127528#post1127528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy answer?<br /> <br /> *Pure Breed is removed*<br /> <br /> What changes?<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs can still rule over the other Garou by &quot;Divine RIght&quot; and their heritage but it's the same way people in RL do t, bullshit culture with no physical manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-11-2017, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:10:31-07:00","id":1127571,"title":"","content":"Coming in late:<br /> <br /> ALL The Rulebooks up to and including W20 so far state that Even <u>Black-F#$%ing-Spiral-Dancers</u> <b>instinctively respect</b> Gaian Garou with High Levels of Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> This brings up problematic notions of race and &quot;purity&quot; in the same way that the Ian Fleming novel &quot;Goldfiner&quot; did; said novel had a <b>sickening</b> scene where Bond angrily tells his Asian Captors &quot;as an English Man, I am entitled to certain privileges, which with my right as a white man I demand NOW!&quot; And his captors meekly obey and give in to his demands for luxury, and only back off when their thoroughly WHITE master Goldfinger, who is not in the LEAST this meek, enters to discuss business with Bond.<br /> <br /> Unless Every Black Spiral lives in a fantasy world of Ian Fleming where &quot;lower&quot; races are brainless and without free will, this notion of &quot;pure breed equals respect and authority&quot; reeks of a sickeningly offensive stupidity that should have been obliterated since the Civil Rights Movement.<br /> <br /> Edit; For that matter: do High Pure Breed Black Spirals also command this instinctive respect in Gaian Garou? Or Fera with Pure breed VS Garou, Vice-Versa Even? I'd imagine Mufasa-Like-Simbas and T-Rex-Like-Mokole of certain pedigree being pretty impressive even to wolves....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 08-11-2017, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T05:37:48-07:00","id":1127581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127571#post1127571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming in late:<br /> <br /> ALL The Rulebooks up to and including W20 so far state that Even <u>Black-F#$%ing-Spiral-Dancers</u> <b>instinctively respect</b> Gaian Garou with High Levels of Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> This brings up problematic notions of race and &quot;purity&quot; in the same way that the Ian Fleming novel &quot;Goldfiner&quot; did; said novel had a <b>sickening</b> scene where Bond angrily tells his Asian Captors &quot;as an English Man, I am entitled to certain privileges, which with my right as a white man I demand NOW!&quot; And his captors meekly obey and give in to his demands for luxury, and only back off when their thoroughly WHITE master Goldfinger, who is not in the LEAST this meek, enters to discuss business with Bond.<br /> <br /> Unless Every Black Spiral lives in a fantasy world of Ian Fleming where &quot;lower&quot; races are brainless and without free will, this notion of &quot;pure breed equals respect and authority&quot; reeks of a sickeningly offensive stupidity that should have been obliterated since the Civil Rights Movement.<br /> <br /> Edit; For that matter: do High Pure Breed Black Spirals also command this instinctive respect in Gaian Garou? Or Fera with Pure breed VS Garou, Vice-Versa Even? I'd imagine Mufasa-Like-Simbas and T-Rex-Like-Mokole of certain pedigree being pretty impressive even to wolves....</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that a Chinese man in the group could have snarled and slapped Bond on the head regardless of his demand. Or brought his OWN breeding to bear. Generally, even if you have breeding, it can only get you so far. And it has little to do with what race you are.<br /> <br /> as for purebred BSDs, yep. They in fact can easily use their breeding to prove they aren't a BSD (since most BSDs are utter mutts). I think with Fera, unless they are part of Ahadi or the Beast Courts, breeding is respected only within breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:45:29-07:00","id":1127627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127581#post1127581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that a Chinese man in the group could have snarled and slapped Bond on the head regardless of his demand. Or brought his OWN breeding to bear. Generally, even if you have breeding, it can only get you so far. And it has little to do with what race you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just using that scene from the book as an analogy of how <b>artificial</b> the notion of &quot;good breeding equals respect&quot; is in ANY Media, gaming table or not.<br /> And Goldfingers Cronies were Korean (whom were the &quot;fashionable to hate&quot; race of Fleming's era).<br /> Point taken all the same.<br /> <br /> And I have a feeling that my Stargazer will <i>continue</i> to get the same &quot;slanty eyed buck toothed thickly-accented Mickey Rooney yellowface impressions&quot; (I hope you burn EXTRA painful in Hell for that role, Mr Rooney) from Fianna, Bone Gnawers and Get Of Fenris as &quot;polite greetings&quot; in particularly conservative American South cities, just like he (and I) did in Melbourne Australia since boyhood, REGARDLESS of his Pure Breed of 5....<br /> Different city, same old Asian hating annoyances.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:41:27-07:00","id":1127661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127571#post1127571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming in late:<br /> <br /> ALL The Rulebooks up to and including W20 so far state that Even <u>Black-F#$%ing-Spiral-Dancers</u> <b>instinctively respect</b> Gaian Garou with High Levels of Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> This brings up problematic notions of race and &quot;purity&quot; in the same way that the Ian Fleming novel &quot;Goldfiner&quot; did; said novel had a <b>sickening</b> scene where Bond angrily tells his Asian Captors &quot;as an English Man, I am entitled to certain privileges, which with my right as a white man I demand NOW!&quot; And his captors meekly obey and give in to his demands for luxury, and only back off when their thoroughly WHITE master Goldfinger, who is not in the LEAST this meek, enters to discuss business with Bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian Fleming was an enormous racist, this is very true. Like Lovecraft people who are his fans have to pretty much read his stuff with a full awareness of these facts. Also, how he routinely will change things to suit his preferences like how Japanese people are completely ****ing awesome unlike other Asian people because Ian liked Japanese culture.<br /> <br /> However, this kind of hits the nail with Pure Breed that you can't be racist against fictional races. You can honestly say orcs are murderous evil Nazis one and all who need to be put to the sword because Orcs don't stand for anyone in real life. They could be whites, blacks, Asians, or orcs because they don't exist. Same as werewolves.<br /> <br /> At least to my knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless Every Black Spiral lives in a fantasy world of Ian Fleming where &quot;lower&quot; races are brainless and without free will, this notion of &quot;pure breed equals respect and authority&quot; reeks of a sickeningly offensive stupidity that should have been obliterated since the Civil Rights Movement.<br /> <br /> Edit; For that matter: do High Pure Breed Black Spirals also command this instinctive respect in Gaian Garou? Or Fera with Pure breed VS Garou, Vice-Versa Even? I'd imagine Mufasa-Like-Simbas and T-Rex-Like-Mokole of certain pedigree being pretty impressive even to wolves.... </div> </div> </div>That's the matter's crux isn't it?<br /> <br /> Basically, everything about Pure Breed screams it's completely shitty. However, does that make it something which should be in the Garou Nation or not? Because the whole thing that made Changeling: The Dreaming interesting for those 9 guys who played it and 20 women was the politics had the Feudalists conquer the Commoner changelings in the 1960s. Which meant, yes, you who had grown up in the United States under democracy were now forced to bend the knee or die to a bunch of elves who GENUINELY had supernatural powers which forced people to acknowledge them as born better.<br /> <br /> God/The Tuatha De Dannan were on their side even if it was bullshit you could reject.<br /> <br /> The problematic element was part of the storytelling.<br /> <br /> Because in both Werewolf and Changeling, being &quot;Born Better&quot; means jack and shit to your ability to rule. It just means people want to make you leader, qualifications nonwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-11-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T10:17:15-07:00","id":1127701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127627#post1127627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I have a feeling that my Stargazer will <i>continue</i> to get the same &quot;slanty eyed buck toothed thickly-accented Mickey Rooney yellowface impressions&quot; (I hope you burn EXTRA painful in Hell for that role, Mr Rooney) from Fianna, Bone Gnawers and Get Of Fenris as &quot;polite greetings&quot; in particularly conservative American South cities, just like he (and I) did in Melbourne Australia since boyhood, REGARDLESS of his Pure Breed of 5....<br /> Different city, same old Asian hating annoyances.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Different areas, different views, unfortunately. I went to school with Somali and other refugees, but I still see racism here in my home country of Finland. But we are trying to learn to be better.<br /> <br /> As @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\">CTPhipps</a> </b>said, purebreed IS shitty but a huge part of the reason why the Nation has so many issues. Just like many dog breed enthusiasts will keep on breeding dogs for looks even if it causes massive health issues and deny there being anything wrong with their dogs, so too will the Silver Fangs and Red Talons point to their breeding as proof of their worth and of Gaia's blessing. But even if the breeding gives them a leg up at first, the pressure to perform is huge. A good ST will not let the character with PB5 just cruise on that stat and will expect them to do the work for having it.<br /> <br /> I do believe purebreed should behave like a CoD merit, in that it has a drawback that actually hurts the character having it.<br /> <br /> Also, to the CtD thing, yes. Sidhe's behaviour and the accordance war are such great story seeds that I am sad CtD didn't focus on it too much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T11:32:18-07:00","id":1127720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127627#post1127627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I have a feeling that my Stargazer will <i>continue</i> to get the same &quot;slanty eyed buck toothed thickly-accented Mickey Rooney yellowface impressions&quot; (I hope you burn EXTRA painful in Hell for that role, Mr Rooney) from Fianna, Bone Gnawers and Get Of Fenris as &quot;polite greetings&quot; in particularly conservative American South cities, just like he (and I) did in Melbourne Australia since boyhood, REGARDLESS of his Pure Breed of 5....<br /> Different city, same old Asian hating annoyances.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't your account recently come off a temporary ban for inflammatory statements like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T11:43:43-07:00","id":1127724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127661#post1127661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the matter's crux isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. Is one of the matters of the crux. There are people who dont like Purebreed as setting element for various reasons. And there are those who dont like it because its rules are plain bad. One group isn't necessarily the other.<br /> <br /> I like PB as a concept but its mechanics are badly designed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T12:16:26-07:00","id":1127737,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I think that there are a bunch of ways in which Pure Breed could function better. For example, if better breeding gave you a better connection to the spirit world while distancing you from the material world, Pure Breed could positively modify the dice pool and difficulty of Gifts and Rites (+1 dice pool for the first level, +1 dice pool and -1 difficulty for the second level, +2 dice pool and -1 difficulty for the third level, +2 dice pool and -2 difficulty for the fourth level, and +3 dice pool and -2 difficulty for the fifth level) at the cost of negatively modifying social interactions with humans and animals, not including Kinfolk (-1 dice pool for the first level, -1 dice pool and +1 difficulty for the second level, -2 dice pool and +1 difficulty for the third level, -2 dice pool and +2 difficulty for the fourth level, and -3 dice pool and +2 difficulty for the fifth level), it would offer a significant advantage that was balanced by a significant disadvantage (Pure Breed for Kinfolk would just apply to their chance of having Fera children). The Silver Fangs would be the leaders of the Garou because they are simply better at Gifts and Rites than most Garou, while the Silver Fang Kinfolk would be involved in business and politics outside of the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-11-2017, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:42:15-07:00","id":1127824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127737#post1127737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I think that there are a bunch of ways in which Pure Breed could function better. For example, if better breeding gave you a better connection to the spirit world while distancing you from the material world</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be more in Spirit Heritage's wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:57:20-07:00","id":1127831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127720#post1127720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't your account recently come off a temporary ban for inflammatory statements like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note how I did NOT cite real life races (Garou Tribes are not races) or specific American Cities in that comment, only personal pain.<br /> <br /> But if that is too vague... (still no specific persons, specific exact places and any specific races)<br /> <br /> 1990s, Melbourne, Australia. A Taiwanese Immigrant boy's Mom's Toyota back-wheel drive was struck by a truck, driven by a epileptic man who had a fit.<br /> A man who should NOT have been given a license for such a dangerous vehicle in the first place because he was epileptic.<br /> <br /> In spite of the fact Mom survived, Said Taiwanese Immigrant Boy went to school, naturally <i>beisde himself with grief...</i><br /> <br /> ...only to be greeted IN HOMEROOM CLASS with not one, not two BUT a swarm of THREE Australian boys who laughed, sang and giggled with their eyes pulled back, exposed &quot;buck teeth&quot; in thick &quot;Japanese&quot; accents &quot;HAHAHAHA! Your Mom's Car Is A Melon! She Shouldn't Have Driven Japanese! You Mom's Car is a Japanese Melon!&quot;<br /> <br /> RIGHT after the day his Mom ALMOST DIED.<br /> <br /> The Australian Teacher was RIGHT THERE, and did jack. That's right. She did NOTHING and just silently smirked.<br /> The Taiwanese Immigrant boy pushed one of the kids back, crying, and told him to stop.<br /> The three Australian Boys suddenly acted scared, didn't even get slaps on the wrists (reassuring rubs across the shoulder actually),<br /> The Taiwanese Immigrant Boy who <i>almost lost his mother</i> got a jolly good screaming to &quot;control his temper&quot; and a jolly good detention as a bonus.<br /> <br /> (Grim smile) Wow, just realized I described the mechanics of how Pure Breed can get you out of trouble by just having enough dots in it in the right situation with the right people (sad coughed laugh)<br /> <br /> Twenty Five Years Later. Never Forgotten. Never Forgiven.<br /> <br /> Portrayals of &quot;Asians&quot; like Mr Rooney's are beloved classics played liberally to fill Family Timeslots back in the 1990's, giving ammunition for those kids on appropriate behavior towards grieving Asian Immigrant Kids who almost lost their parents. I'm sorry if the &quot;burn in Hell&quot; statement offended people here, but hopefully it should be clear that the Taiwanese Immigrant boy would therefore owe Mr Rooney no respect whatsoever.<br /> <br /> No specific persons or races of said three bullies were named,<br /> They will remain perfectly fine, safe and unmolested still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 08-11-2017, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:19:53-07:00","id":1128013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1127571#post1127571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) Unless Every Black Spiral... (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you recommend any Wt:A books in regards to game sessions in which the Black Spiral Dancers are involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:32:32-07:00","id":1128634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see nothing wrong with that. Its cutting the problematic mechanic all together. And it can affect common gameplay outside of the act of breeding. For example in certain negotiations or dealings with tribes that care specially about strong family lines but what it wouldnt be is an abolute &quot;this works always like this regardless of context&quot; kind of mechanic </div> </div> </div>I'd rather try to fix the mechanic with something less of a win condition. That said, in my current campaign pure breed (4 and 2 on two different characters) has honestly still to give the players a real advantage, since most of their social rolls happened with humans, in towns... so yea, I recognize that it's strong but it only helps with the garou and won't help much anyway against an angry elder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PB is a type of classicism there is no question about it. It doesnt make the game &quot;bad&quot; because of it because its part of the game the fight against said classicism. Its part of the conflict and is there. But the big majority of people that have issue with it dont do that because of the classicism but because the mechanics of it are trainwreck of poor design. </div> </div> </div>I have no issues with complains about poor design, I'd just rather not have discussion on how racism is wrong here. It's a gaming forum and we're talking about a game, so who cares. =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:44:54-07:00","id":1130380,"title":"","content":"I just came back to the forum from a long absence and to be honest, haven't really read the whole 8 page thread on Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> However, I kind of hate Pure Breed, though I do like the &quot;Great things are expected from you&quot; aspect of the background. Also Pure Breed never made much sense for tribes like the Children of Gaia who accepted outcasts and didn't enforce arranged marriages.<br /> <br /> This is how I house ruled it in my game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In an effort to make social status in the game less about eugenics/appearance and more about being descended from heroes, we will be removing Pure Breed from the game and changing how Notable Heritage Merit works. Notable Heritage will not be tied to a specific tribe, but to family lines created by the player. The Fortunes of Family Lines can rise and fall and Garou with no notable family history can found new lines of heroes.<br /> <br /> Your PC could come from a line of Black Furies but if they join the Children of Gaia, they do no lose their Notable Heritage. Your Get of Fenris could look like a Red Talon or really whatever wolf makes sense for their background without having to spend points on it.<br /> <br /> There will now be two levels of Notable Heritage, a 3 point and a 5 point merit. Each point ranking of the merit still adds to rank challenges and social rolls involving Garou and Kinfolk (Even Ronin and Black Spiral Dancers).<br /> <br /> <b>Notable Heritage (3 Points)</b> - Your character descends from the heroes of the Garou Nation. Other characters tell you how you look just like your father/mother/great aunt and expect great things from you. Stories are told of how your great grandmother, Bays at the Moon, bested the wretched Black Spiral Dance, Back of My Hand, in combat. Please list at least one notable ancestor of at least Adren/Athro in Rank in your Character History and add public information about your ancestor to the Silver Record.<br /> <br /> <b>Notable Heritage (5 Points) </b>- Your character descends from the leaders of the Garou Nation. Other characters tell you how you look just like your father/mother and expect great things from you. Sept Alphas and Tribal Elders can be found up your family tree. Please list at least one notable ancestor of at least Elder/Legend in Rank in your Character History and add public information about your ancestor to the Silver Record.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Tribal Restrictions</u><br /> <br /> Silver Fangs - All Silver Fang Characters must have Notable Heritage at the five point level. Falcon only accepts those Garou that are descended from the leaders of the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers - Notable Heritage is restricted for all Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker Characters. Both Urban Tribes are focused on what your character accomplished rather than what your ancestors did. </div> </div> </div>The side effect of this change meant there was a LOT less Notable Heritage in our game. Pure Breed is suppose to be rare, but it seemed every PC in a non Pure Breed Restricted Tribe had some. With this house rule, it was more work on the player to add a Notable ancestor to their background and thus made the Merit more rare. I even dropped it from some of my NPCs cause I couldn't think of a suitable ancestor for them.<br /> <br /> For those who did take Notable Heritage, it added an extra dimension to their character. Instead of Pure Breed being dots on a sheet, the other PCs treated the Notable Heritage characters differently because they KNEW the story behind their ancestors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 08-17-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:49:48-07:00","id":1130455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130380#post1130380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The side effect of this change meant there was a LOT less Notable Heritage in our game. Pure Breed is suppose to be rare, but it seemed every PC in a non Pure Breed Restricted Tribe had some.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've rarely seen Pure Breed used in table top. Even the players who pick SF tribe for their PC seems reluctant to give up precious build points on Pure Breed. Once they get to the more supernatural Backgrounds, most PCs prefer Totem (by far), Rites (especially for certain auspices), or even Ancestors or Fetish. They want to use their Background points and Freebies on other things. But everyone's game is different.<br /> <br /> The only place I see Pure Breed picked by many players is in LARP and Online roleplay because most social interaction there is with other PCs and not the ST plot or NPCs. That's no different from players making sure they have a tag showing Glamorous x5 pinned to their shirt, or picking an attractive model for their online model of their character.<br /> <br /> PCs, of course, are always special and will do whatever. I've long given up trying to police them during character creation unless they do something spectacularly off basis. When it comes to setting limitations (such as Pure Breed is rare), I concentrate on the NPCs and the setting as a whole. Not the PCs. Usually once I know their general concept and character creation choices, I will drive them to things so I can better have them make sense in the chronicle. (OK, you will be playing a Pure Breed 4 SF, which of these three SF NPC families would you like your character to belong to. Hmm, you are playing a high Pure Breed Black Fury, let's figure out together the best way we incorporate that into the setting, and by the way since none of the other Black Furies have anywhere near your PB, it'll become an important element in play.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130380#post1130380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this house rule, it was more work on the player to add a Notable ancestor to their background and thus made the Merit more rare. I even dropped it from some of my NPCs cause I couldn't think of a suitable ancestor for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I see with your house rule is that given the small number of Garou and kinfolk in the world (especially once you get down to single tribes as individual populations), their oral traditions, and ancestral memory, I would think almost any Garou would eventually be able to find one or more notable ancestors very quickly. One in every 12.5 people in Asia (and one in 200 worldwide) can claim descent from Genghis Khan. There's around ten other men just as successful as he was. Then you have lots of other people who could be called notable that just weren't as successful genetically. And of course Garou don't just judge the male ancestor as being notable, but also the female one. Even if you take people outside the tribe and begin breeding with them, and thus that half of their family has zero notable Garou ancestors, the other half could be extremely notable.<br /> <br /> There is also the issue of the Ancestors ability versus the Pure Breed. I've seen PCs with almost no Pure Breed but lots of Ancestors. And those ancestors (especially distant ones) they contact could be quite notable. It's just that the PC doesn't appear to be like them at all.<br /> <br /> Physical similarity between siblings, cousins, and parents is something often remarked on. Is there any father who isn't told that their newborn baby looks like him; or finding various things they can match back to others (she has Grandmom's curly hair, or eyes like Great Aunt Sally)? Or if you see photos of past family generations and notice that only a certain grandson or great grandson still has similarities to the original family patriarch, then that is something the family as a whole mentions. Or in big extended family get togethers how you pierce who is who (&quot;You can tell he's one of the Hartwells because he has thin lips&quot;). Other times it may not be something physical, but another trait (&quot;he has the typical Johnson sense of humor&quot; or &quot;she has the fiery temper of her mother's side of the family&quot;) <br /> <br /> So personally, I like the idea that there is a physical aspect or other trait that is associated with &quot;Pure Breed&quot; that others recognize. It's not just that someone is descended from some notable Garou (who isn't if you go back enough in time?). It's the idea that right here, right now, it seems that someone from that Golden Age of Heroes is with us.<br /> <br /> I think what hampers some people is the idea that there is ONE ideal way of looking. If you are told Silver Fangs are supposed to have blond hair, blue eyes, and pale skin, that is very limiting. So I've never done it that way. Certain lineages may be known for that, but others do not. Silver Fangs from House Wise Heart or House Blood Red Crest don't look like Nordics, but people from their native region. I also have members of the more European based Crescent Moon hail from the Uralic or Siberian peoples. Their notable features may come in the form of bushy eyebrows, keen eyesight, oddly shaped birthmarks, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed isn't something obviously physical because it's not noticed by humans or even kinfolk. It's a factor from the Garou's spirit side as a result of their totem. What the Garou sense is something instinctive that would be hard to put into words because human language cannot refer to it. (Just had the idea that it might be possible to brainstorm with your players new nonsense words that refer to Pure Breed traits to make up for that. &quot;Oh, look you can tell he's very <i>lurr</i>. I wonder if he's part of that renown Fianna lineage?&quot; And then you define what &quot;lurr&quot; is, like someone who has the noble aspect of a buck deer trotting in the autumn leaves, or someone with the eyes of a predator looking for an escaped prey). So physical appearance is one aspect, and often defaults simply to those kind of traits that typically announce someone is healthy genetically. It's just that there are also other things outside of that which only Garou could sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130380#post1130380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who did take Notable Heritage, it added an extra dimension to their character. Instead of Pure Breed being dots on a sheet, the other PCs treated the Notable Heritage characters differently because they KNEW the story behind their ancestors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in general whenever PCs or ST actually do more work creating flavor text for the dots on their character sheet, the other players become more engaged. Many players put a lot of work into their individual character's backstory, but I find most players don't want to put any effort in detailing those aspects if their character sheet immediately outside of them. Allies and Contacts are supposed to have a specific number of &quot;major&quot; Allies and Contacts that should be detailed, but players don't want to put the effort into a brief one to two sentence synopsis. Likewise with kinfolk, I don't see players who want to identify any outside the immediate family of their character. If a player picks a Fetish, it is a generic utilitarian fetish - despite the fact it should have a very well known history and lore behind it.<br /> <br /> Most players simply want to handwave those details. But whenever one puts effort into detailing something, it almost always adds greatly to the game because those individual touches become an important part of that chronicle's lore. Far more important than detailed work the ST does because it is always directly relevant to the PCs in a way the ST's NPCs, items, and events may not be.<br /> <br /> I generally ask my players if they have Backgrounds that involve NPCs, that they put some effort into detailing them. So if they have Allies, Contacts, and Kinfolk, who are they? If they have Pure Breed, provide some details on that lineage. If they have Ancestors, who are some of their ancestors they contact? I even ask them to put down what spirit taught them each of their Gifts. Stuff like that fills out the game world nicely as you noted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:47:33-07:00","id":1130589,"title":"","content":"With online games, the biggest issue with purebreed there is that players -want- to have breeding for the story. But often they don't actually want to play their character by the breeding nor do the STs actually put the PCs to task about it. Another issue is that a lot of players who DO play the pompous noble Fang often are way too serious about their character succeeding and getting flak for acting like a douche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:07:53-07:00","id":1130670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130380#post1130380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I house ruled it in my game:</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont see any change beyond an expectation of deciding on the PC whole family tree before the game starts. Still is OP as fuck, as you can use it on formal challenges (that include combat) and social rolls against Garou and Kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130455#post1130455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've rarely seen Pure Breed used in table top. Even the players who pick SF tribe for their PC seems reluctant to give up precious build points on Pure Breed. Once they get to the more supernatural Backgrounds, most PCs prefer Totem (by far), Rites (especially for certain auspices), or even Ancestors or Fetish. They want to use their Background points and Freebies on other things. But everyone's game is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my case, is the most common build i see is to Boost PB to 4 or 5 if you are a SF or a Fenrir and use it to boost all your social gifts. Buy some flaws to compensate. And buy enchanting voice and then really REALLY break the game in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-18-2017, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T14:42:03-07:00","id":1130977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130589#post1130589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With online games, the biggest issue with purebreed there is that players -want- to have breeding for the story. But often they don't actually want to play their character by the breeding nor do the STs actually put the PCs to task about it. Another issue is that a lot of players who DO play the pompous noble Fang often are way too serious about their character succeeding and getting flak for acting like a douche.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you want the player characters to be NORMAL examples of a tribe then you're STing wrong. That was always a weird thing about WOD games where everyone was angry about characters going too off concept but player characters should be, ultimately, unique compared to most other tribes.<br /> <br /> Even if, yes, that means they're a gentle hearted (but still tough) Get of Fenris or the sympathetic humble Silver Fang.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T15:10:15-07:00","id":1130984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130977#post1130977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you want the player characters to be NORMAL examples of a tribe then you're STing wrong. That was always a weird thing about WOD games where everyone was angry about characters going too off concept but player characters should be, ultimately, unique compared to most other tribes.<br /> <br /> Even if, yes, that means they're a gentle hearted (but still tough) Get of Fenris or the sympathetic humble Silver Fang.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a table top game this is fine since the ST populates the entire rest of the world and can make it look like it is in canon (or their version of it).<br /> <br /> In online games and big LARPs, being <i>laissez faire</i> on character creation will quickly get you a chronicle of homid Red Talons, at least five White Howlers, a Croatan, Bone Gnawers who are really lost Silver Fang princesses, a redeemed Black Spiral Dancer, and twenty lupus Stargazers as your standard sept. Many PCs want their character to be special, but most players hate playing in a game where everyone is a unique snowflake (regardless of whether their character is). That's why most of those games put various restrictions in place or caps on certain concepts in an attempt to have their chronicle vaguely resemble people's expectations (how it is described in canon).<br /> <br /> In practice this has middling results because STs have to balance keeping a lid on ridiculous things and keeping an active player base.<br /> <br /> But it is a different dynamic STing a small table top game with a closed playing group and an open online or LARP chronicle with lots of players, many of whom can be brand new. So the ST style needs to be very different to accommodate those differences.<br /> <br /> But I agree it was particularly weird to read in actual White Wolf published material that &quot;you are doing it wrong!&quot;. It would have been far better to just ignore the weird stuff players did, and simply publish a very good setting book showing how it is supposed to be done. Instead, they just kept introducing more and more weird stuff and then complained when playing groups actually used those concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-19-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:45:15-07:00","id":1131119,"title":"","content":"As an ST and a player in TT, I want interesting PCs. Part of the problem with, &quot;expect the PCs to be wildly off Tribal concept for TT play,&quot; is that it gets boring really fast when you see the same &quot;iconoclast&quot; concepts over any over because people mistake non-normal concepts for things that are actually interesting (and therefore fun) to play.<br /> <br /> One thing I always try to stress in my TT games is that you get the most fun with characters that play with the splats you pick, rather than directly work against them. A character that seems to be a normal member of their Tribe can hide all sorts of hidden depths that make them something rare, and a character that seems like a strange fit for a Tribe can actually be someone that upholds their ideals in amazing ways. But pacifist Fenrir and Red Talon business owners get boring if all they are, are contradictions of the stereotypes of their Tribes. Anti-stereotypes are just as boring to play as stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T04:38:30-07:00","id":1131184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1130977#post1130977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think if you want the player characters to be NORMAL examples of a tribe then you're STing wrong. That was always a weird thing about WOD games where everyone was angry about characters going too off concept but player characters should be, ultimately, unique compared to most other tribes.<br /> <br /> Even if, yes, that means they're a gentle hearted (but still tough) Get of Fenris or the sympathetic humble Silver Fang.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, more allowing characters aren't the issue as much. It is that often they are -all- there is. In TT, this wouldn't be an issue, but when you got 20 Silver Fangs who are all humble and accepting, it can get boring.<br /> <br /> Besides, it isn't that stereotypical characters are bad, it is that often their players don't want to actually play by the established canon of the forum/chat/MUSH and get pissed off when their characters get treated as jerks. Players who realise that their PCs are playing the antagonist or the rivial role often last much longer, as they can play by that role. Such characters are needed, because they keep the conflict going among the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:39:34-07:00","id":1131213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131119#post1131119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an ST and a player in TT, I want interesting PCs. Part of the problem with, &quot;expect the PCs to be wildly off Tribal concept for TT play,&quot; is that it gets boring really fast when you see the same &quot;iconoclast&quot; concepts over any over because people mistake non-normal concepts for things that are actually interesting (and therefore fun) to play.<br /> <br /> One thing I always try to stress in my TT games is that you get the most fun with characters that play with the splats you pick, rather than directly work against them. A character that seems to be a normal member of their Tribe can hide all sorts of hidden depths that make them something rare, and a character that seems like a strange fit for a Tribe can actually be someone that upholds their ideals in amazing ways. But pacifist Fenrir and Red Talon business owners get boring if all they are, are contradictions of the stereotypes of their Tribes. Anti-stereotypes are just as boring to play as stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, it's a Gothic Punk setting so iconoclast is supposed to be good. After all, all of the tribes are deliberately written as being screwed up. That's just my take, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:22:21-07:00","id":1131412,"title":"","content":"Sure, but that's why I put &quot;iconoclast&quot; in quotes in my post. A strong iconoclastic character is going to be more than an anti-stereotype. This is especially true for Tribe, where the Tribes initiate you, which means they'd rarely bring you into the fold if you're going to be fighting them the whole way (even PB can't be used as an excuse here, because PB that's not empowered by the Tribal Totem of the character's heritage doesn't do anything).<br /> <br /> A Black Fury that's a modern third wave feminist that struggles against the TERF-y second wave elders of the Tribe is a good iconoclastic character, because they're playing into the issues of the Tribal philosophy. A male Metis Black Fury that's an adamant MRA... is just too much of an anti-stereotype to work as a good iconoclast. The Furies are never going to accept such a person in their ranks for them to actually struggle against the Tribal authority.<br /> <br /> There's a fine line between subverting stereotypes, and making a cliched stereotype that's just different from the stereotype you're trying to subvert.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:47:24-07:00","id":1131450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131213#post1131213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, it's a Gothic Punk setting so iconoclast is supposed to be good. After all, all of the tribes are deliberately written as being screwed up. That's just my take, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, if everyone is iconoclast, no one is. That is the issue. If all 20 of the silver fang pcs in the chat are modern open-minded hipsters, how much does that showcase the tribe's flaws of being stuck in the old ways and being dismissing of the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T16:51:03-07:00","id":1131511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131450#post1131450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, if everyone is iconoclast, no one is. That is the issue. If all 20 of the silver fang pcs in the chat are modern open-minded hipsters, how much does that showcase the tribe's flaws of being stuck in the old ways and being dismissing of the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you tell them they should form a Lodge.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T00:55:41-07:00","id":1131648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131511#post1131511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you tell them they should form a Lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you tell them to play another tribe. Crafting a white fly is the most abused and trite narrative trick to craft a &quot;different&quot; character, because it's so easy that everyone can think about it. Make a Get of Fenris and have him not acting like a GoF, here's a cool character for you! It's such a clich\u00e9 that from a literary standpoint it marks the author as &quot;bad&quot; just for using it, and I discourage my players every time they try to create this kind of character. If you want to play a pacifist then you play a Child of Gaia, not a Fenris.<br /> Of course, some storyteller may feel perfectly fine with white flies, especially when they raise the banner of some particular cause they believe in (like equalitarists Silver Fangs). But it's your campaign, so if it doesn't bother you or your players I see no issue in playing it however you like. In a tabletop game isn't even that harmful, since it's 4 players against a world of stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Thing is, though, that this kind of &quot;versus&quot; character is horribly harmful in a multiplayer online game. Partly because they break the game lore (potentially ruining the setting to other players), but also because they are the kind of character that lives on the shoulder of the others. When your toon's personality is to be against the status quo then he doesn't have a personality, he's just leeching some from the action of others by disrupting their gameplay.<br /> This may lead to some fun when controlled: the single thief in a city can offer a lot. But when half of the city is made by thieves they become harmful to the game world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:12:10-07:00","id":1131722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131648#post1131648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, you tell them to play another tribe. Crafting a white fly is the most abused and trite narrative trick to craft a &quot;different&quot; character, because it's so easy that everyone can think about it. Make a Get of Fenris and have him not acting like a GoF, here's a cool character for you! It's such a clich\u00e9 that from a literary standpoint it marks the author as &quot;bad&quot; just for using it, and I discourage my players every time they try to create this kind of character. If you want to play a pacifist then you play a Child of Gaia, not a Fenris.<br /> Of course, some storyteller may feel perfectly fine with white flies, especially when they raise the banner of some particular cause they believe in (like equalitarists Silver Fangs). But it's your campaign, so if it doesn't bother you or your players I see no issue in playing it however you like. In a tabletop game isn't even that harmful, since it's 4 players against a world of stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Thing is, though, that this kind of &quot;versus&quot; character is horribly harmful in a multiplayer online game. Partly because they break the game lore (potentially ruining the setting to other players), but also because they are the kind of character that lives on the shoulder of the others. When your toon's personality is to be against the status quo then he doesn't have a personality, he's just leeching some from the action of others by disrupting their gameplay.<br /> This may lead to some fun when controlled: the single thief in a city can offer a lot. But when half of the city is made by thieves they become harmful to the game world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two thoughts on this matter:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Just because you're not the first to do something shouldn't make your choice to do it be treated that much worse. Sure, someone <i>was</i> the first to write Drizzt, that doesn't mean that others should not be given the opportunity to have all the fun.</li> <li>Are you sure that the stereotypes are based on truth? If 19 out of 20 tribe members turn out to mismatch their stereotypes, maybe the problem is not that they mismatch the stereotypes, but rather that the onlooker making the observation is a misinformed tribe-ist? After all, how many people had stereotypes about Jews, or USAians, or Japanese, only to find that their expectations don't match their actual experience with actual living members of those groups? Given that Garou tribes are in many ways reminiscent of nations, I think that's fitting.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:09:08-07:00","id":1131737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131722#post1131722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two thoughts on this matter:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Just because you're not the first to do something shouldn't make your choice to do it be treated that much worse. Sure, someone <i>was</i> the first to write Drizzt, that doesn't mean that others should not be given the opportunity to have all the fun.</li> <li>Are you sure that the stereotypes are based on truth? If 19 out of 20 tribe members turn out to mismatch their stereotypes, maybe the problem is not that they mismatch the stereotypes, but rather that the onlooker making the observation is a misinformed tribe-ist? After all, how many people had stereotypes about Jews, or USAians, or Japanese, only to find that their expectations don't match their actual experience with actual living members of those groups? Given that Garou tribes are in many ways reminiscent of nations, I think that's fitting.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean, my issue -isn't- that there are open minded Fangs or Fenrir or arsehole Children of Gaia. My issue is that often those are the -only- characters found in the games and as such it doesn't bring up a good conversation on the nature of the tribe.<br /> <br /> As for the stereotypes, minus Black Furies, they to me always felt like how america saw the various ethnic groups/sub-cultures. Fenrir as neo-nazi, Fianna as irish drunks, Bone Gnawers as drunk bums,etc. At least in the 1st edition and 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Thing in play is, though, that some stereotypes are true. Silver Fang culture DOES support insane amount of separation between them and the rest of the Nation because they are the leaders. Red Talons do kill humans. Some Children of Gaia do lack the moral backbone to be true warriors and some Black Furies sacrifice male babies in rituals. Point is, tribes aren't good or bad, they are both. And without there being a good balance of both, a lot of the good stuff that could be explored by the game is lost.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reason I play metis from traditional tribes. Because they bring up discussions of the Nation's wrongs, or believe in very disturbing traditions. Yet are still victims of the system.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:05:41-07:00","id":1131787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131648#post1131648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, you tell them to play another tribe. Crafting a white fly is the most abused and trite narrative trick to craft a &quot;different&quot; character, because it's so easy that everyone can think about it. Make a Get of Fenris and have him not acting like a GoF, here's a cool character for you! It's such a clich\u00e9 that from a literary standpoint it marks the author as &quot;bad&quot; just for using it, and I discourage my players every time they try to create this kind of character. If you want to play a pacifist then you play a Child of Gaia, not a Fenris.<br /> Of course, some storyteller may feel perfectly fine with white flies, especially when they raise the banner of some particular cause they believe in (like equalitarists Silver Fangs). But it's your campaign, so if it doesn't bother you or your players I see no issue in playing it however you like. In a tabletop game isn't even that harmful, since it's 4 players against a world of stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Thing is, though, that this kind of &quot;versus&quot; character is horribly harmful in a multiplayer online game. Partly because they break the game lore (potentially ruining the setting to other players), but also because they are the kind of character that lives on the shoulder of the others. When your toon's personality is to be against the status quo then he doesn't have a personality, he's just leeching some from the action of others by disrupting their gameplay.<br /> This may lead to some fun when controlled: the single thief in a city can offer a lot. But when half of the city is made by thieves they become harmful to the game world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm going to say no for that. At least at my table.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to play a Silver Fang then they should be able to. If you have a room full of nonasshole Silver Fang then you should play that as the ST.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are all people who share the same beliefs but NO ONE ELSE IN THE TRIBE&quot; shares them.<br /> <br /> The fact they're a group of such believers should be incorporated into the narrative unless the players are uncomfortable with the fact they're not special snowflakes with the others around.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:40:34-07:00","id":1132006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131787#post1131787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm going to say no for that. At least at my table.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to play a Silver Fang then they should be able to. If you have a room full of nonasshole Silver Fang then you should play that as the ST.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are all people who share the same beliefs but NO ONE ELSE IN THE TRIBE&quot; shares them.<br /> <br /> The fact they're a group of such believers should be incorporated into the narrative unless the players are uncomfortable with the fact they're not special snowflakes with the others around.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the fact that in long term, it can lead to a pretty nasty habit from the forum runners. Unless a sept is specifically written as non-white based, there tends to be Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords leading it. Most who are accepting and open minded. Which to me is not that good of a thing, as it kinda gives a bad message about them. A sort of 'well, THEY are nice and he is a fair leader, guess the Fangs are okay', which underlines the whole schism between them and the Nation. Plus, as most septs are set in America and most Fang NPCs (and PCs) are european stock, it kiinda also goes into uncomfortable territory with its implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:04:46-07:00","id":1132014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132006#post1132006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is also the fact that in long term, it can lead to a pretty nasty habit from the forum runners. Unless a sept is specifically written as non-white based, there tends to be Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords leading it. Most who are accepting and open minded. Which to me is not that good of a thing, as it kinda gives a bad message about them. A sort of 'well, THEY are nice and he is a fair leader, guess the Fangs are okay', which underlines the whole schism between them and the Nation. Plus, as most septs are set in America and most Fang NPCs (and PCs) are european stock, it kiinda also goes into uncomfortable territory with its implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, that's actually an in-game problem isn't it? The Silver Fangs are the &quot;rulers&quot; in America because they took over their lands and conquered them with genocide as well as slaughter just like happened with the real work.<br /> <br /> Which is part of the 1E Werewolf conflict between the Pure Lands tribes and Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> The modern ones are a lot nicer than the older ones but does that make up for anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:29:06-07:00","id":1132026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132014#post1132014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, that's actually an in-game problem isn't it? The Silver Fangs are the &quot;rulers&quot; in America because they took over their lands and conquered them with genocide as well as slaughter just like happened with the real work.<br /> <br /> Which is part of the 1E Werewolf conflict between the Pure Lands tribes and Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> The modern ones are a lot nicer than the older ones but does that make up for anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>If would be a great in-game problem, if it was done on purpose. It is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:31:28-07:00","id":1132030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132026#post1132026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If would be a great in-game problem, if it was done on purpose. It is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused, how is it not on purpose?<br /> <br /> I mean the Wendigo and Uktena hating the Europeans is everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T00:05:48-07:00","id":1132109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132030#post1132030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused, how is it not on purpose?<br /> <br /> I mean the Wendigo and Uktena hating the Europeans is everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant from the STs that run the games. If the fact that Fangs were running the sept was meant to showcase the unfair taking of septs, that would be cool. But the reasons Fangs are leaders is often because they are cool and these Fangs are often very allowing and open minded. That is why there is no real support to that narrative from the game's perspective.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T01:45:53-07:00","id":1132122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1131722#post1131722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you're not the first to do something shouldn't make your choice to do it be treated that much worse. Sure, someone <i>was</i> the first to write Drizzt, that doesn't mean that others should not be given the opportunity to have all the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, my point was that Drizz't is a stupid character that harms the setting. You should not have even one Drizz't to begin with, having five on a total of thirty drows is just disruptive.<br /> How many times have I seen teen players telling a Drow matron to get bent? It's nonsensical, and somehow they even cried when the matron executed them on spot. How many of them ask for their backstory to be: &quot;Yes, my character told an ilharess to shut up and attacked her, and he managed to kill her swiftly, and he fled from Menzoberranzan and now lives in the human world&quot;? My answer, usually, is &quot;No, your character was captured two minutes later and died after two years of torture and captivity. Now he's a zombie servant of the matrons&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want a drow to play it like a human then play a human. And guess what, it's a lot harder than playing a humanized drow since you actually have to think at something to give it spice and personality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you sure that the stereotypes are based on truth? If 19 out of 20 tribe members turn out to mismatch their stereotypes, maybe the problem is not that they mismatch the stereotypes, but rather that the onlooker making the observation is a misinformed tribe-ist? After all, how many people had stereotypes about Jews, or USAians, or Japanese, only to find that their expectations don't match their actual experience with actual living members of those groups? Given that Garou tribes are in many ways reminiscent of nations, I think that's fitting. </div> </div> </div>Stereotypes weren't the point either. Of course I don't want stereotyped characters, how boring can it be to have only drunkards as Fianna?<br /> I mean, after all Albrecht is REALLY an innovator for the Fangs, so it's not like you need to be an asshole stuck in the past. I'm just saying that a good character should fit his tribe. After all your character chose it for a reason, and the totem accepted you because you were within the parameters (i.e., Fenris would not accept garous that shy away from combat).<br /> <br /> A special mention could be made for Silver Fangs or everyone that picks the tribe because of their ancestors (my fathers were Fianna, so I'm going to be a Fianna too), and on how such characters may harbour a different worldview but be accepted anyway because of their blood; if they stayed in the tribe, though, they should at least value their history and traditions, so it would make sense for them to not be THAT much against the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone wants to play a Silver Fang then they should be able to. If you have a room full of nonasshole Silver Fang then you should play that as the ST. </div> </div> </div>Without repeating myself on the stereotypes, surely you can do that. But if I have four players and one of them is annoyed by the idea that another one wants to play a marxist Silver Fang then I'm going to sink the second one, because even if I can bend the setting to accomodate their ideas (even when childish: it's all for fun, after all) I won't do it if it's going to make someone else uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> If someone wants to be a starship captain in the Forgotten Realms I surely can accomodate the campaign to make them the crew of the Enterprise that shift into a different Material Plane, but if even one of them yells &quot;I want none of this bullshit&quot; then I won't. Everyone has the right to ask that the agreed theme of the game is respected (and that includes the Storyteller, mind you: he has the right to have fun just like the others); you can always pick a different setting, after all, if the space theme is more appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 08-21-2017, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T07:08:56-07:00","id":1132201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132109#post1132109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant from the STs that run the games. If the fact that Fangs were running the sept was meant to showcase the unfair taking of septs, that would be cool. But the reasons Fangs are leaders is often because they are cool and these Fangs are often very allowing and open minded. That is why there is no real support to that narrative from the game's perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well are we talking about PCs or NPCs?<br /> <br /> Because PCs being open minded progressive Silver Fangs isn't something which should be a problem because that's out of the ST's hands. If it's NPCs that's up to the ST. No one should be encouraged, save in-game, to be a dick just to fit a tribal stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T07:19:35-07:00","id":1132204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132122#post1132122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, my point was that Drizz't is a stupid character that harms the setting. You should not have even one Drizz't to begin with, having five on a total of thirty drows is just disruptive.<br /> How many times have I seen teen players telling a Drow matron to get bent? It's nonsensical, and somehow they even cried when the matron executed them on spot. How many of them ask for their backstory to be: &quot;Yes, my character told an ilharess to shut up and attacked her, and he managed to kill her swiftly, and he fled from Menzoberranzan and now lives in the human world&quot;? My answer, usually, is &quot;No, your character was captured two minutes later and died after two years of torture and captivity. Now he's a zombie servant of the matrons&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want a drow to play it like a human then play a human. And guess what, it's a lot harder than playing a humanized drow since you actually have to think at something to give it spice and personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're getting into the issue of &quot;Incredibly disruptive players&quot; which is a different issue than &quot;Special Snowflake Syndrome.&quot; I've had players who have wanted to play Highlander Immortals, a Justicar who drove around in a forklift, and a human trained by a Predator so I know people who really take it to the next level of disrupting the game. And yes, sometimes I bring down the &quot;Do you want to play the game or not?&quot; on them because it would destroy everything cool about it. I actually convinced one problematic friend in RL to play a straight Toreador Neonate and see if he enjoyed doing the &quot;right&quot; way by playing all the horror and shock. It worked and he's now one of my best players. He just made a Lost Cub Silver Fang lesbian runaway who is horrified by Garou traditions but struggling to fit in.<br /> <br /> BE THAT AS IT MAY, the reason people made so many Drizzt clones is because the character has an awesome easy to understand backstory. No one is playing Dungeons and Dragons just to be generic fighter dude if they can be someone with a rich epic backstory who does make an impression. People who play RPGs for the roleplaying element want to do something memorable and fascinating which I often feel is a problem of not entirely trusting the ST. I think it was something like, &quot;I made this epic backstory for my player character because I don't think I'm ever going to do anything half as memorable in game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, I figured how they did it in Forgotten Realms was clever. They made a God of Good Drow and a God of Rebels for the Drow so PCs could theoretically all be Drizzt clones without being ridiculous--notably, R.A. Salvator HATED that because it did remove DRIZZT'S uniqueness.<br /> <br /> But yes, I've run &quot;The Last Croatoan&quot; and &quot;secretly Black Spiral Dancer purebreed&quot; before with minimal fuss. Albretch is a good example also of how to do a Silver Fang who is completely lacking renown in his Tribe (pre-SIlver Crown of course) and still a nominal member of the tribe. Yes, &quot;Homeless Bum&quot; Silver Fang isn't the way the tribe is normally played but if the player is up for it, they can be a figure of pity or anger from their tribe or having been driven to that because of past politics. You can also do the rich Bone Gnawer who is considered a sell out and loathed by his kinfolk as well as kinsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T07:22:00-07:00","id":1132205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132201#post1132201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well are we talking about PCs or NPCs?<br /> <br /> Because PCs being open minded progressive Silver Fangs isn't something which should be a problem because that's out of the ST's hands. If it's NPCs that's up to the ST. No one should be encouraged, save in-game, to be a dick just to fit a tribal stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>NPCs of course, usually these white haired models used as pictures, too. Generally, the issue is that these guys are open minded and fair, thus not giving the Fangs players an opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T11:37:57-07:00","id":1132316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132205#post1132205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> NPCs of course, usually these white haired models used as pictures, too. Generally, the issue is that these guys are open minded and fair, thus not giving the Fangs players an opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is up to the ST.<br /> <br /> But yes, I would make generally all authority figures but Albretch complete tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T14:08:43-07:00","id":1132388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1123755-pure-breed-problem?p=1132316#post1132316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that is up to the ST.<br /> <br /> But yes, I would make generally all authority figures but Albretch complete tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is the issue, because the Fang NPCs are (mostly) treated as open minded and accepting, the PCs AND players treat them taking caerns with a lot less issues than they should. By that, the Fangs pcs who are accepting won't face any opposition from their Elders.<br /> <br /> And this leads into the high purebreed of these PCs basically existing only to add to their dice rolls, with no expectations from the tribe to live up to the legends.<br /> <br /> At worst, it leads into these heroic blonde and blue eyed people basically being most of the sept's population, with any non-Fangs being either loyal Fenrir/Fianna/Gnawers/Lords by their side. Or anyone not liking it being treated awfully IC and OOC for being like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}